INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('818729b7-51fc-4534-b15f-09404f8978dc','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Atlas normal path.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/818729b7-51fc-4534-b15f-09404f8978dc.mp3','REG-ATLAS2',2,'message','bm_george','2026-06-08T13:42:20.726Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('98b95ec1-93bd-49fd-9180-63917bacce1d','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Got it. Here''s what I''m doing. The Offers page is actually your homepage, and the basket page doesn''t even exist yet — the menu links to it but it four-oh-fours. So: I''m stripping the Offers homepage and the basket page down to a single centered word, like you asked — Offers, and My Basket — dropping the full template on both. I''m renaming the Dutch routes to English: vergelijken becomes compare, and mandje becomes basket. The menu item for the basket I''m labeling My List, like you said. The compare page itself, the real search, I''m leaving fully working, just moving it to the English URL. One naming flag: the menu will say My List but the page heading says My Basket and the URL is slash-basket — if you want all three to read the same word, tell me which and I''ll unify in one pass. Building and verifying once it''s wired.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/98b95ec1-93bd-49fd-9180-63917bacce1d.mp3','ENGLISH ROUTES + PLACEHOLDERS',41,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T13:42:45.459Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('65ce301a-8d65-4729-b4c3-390d9470cdc0','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Done — pai-voice is now hardened and I verified it the hard way. resolveAgent can no longer throw on a bad agent: a missing, malformed, voiceless, or stale persona name now degrades to Ringo, and if even Ringo''s config were gone it falls back to built-in Ringo defaults. I proved every one of those paths live, including deleting ringo''s config to force the last-resort branch, then restored it. I also added a path-traversal guard on the agent name. Forge audited the whole thing read-only and passed it: no throw path left, the normal Atlas and Ringo paths are unchanged, and nothing leaks to stdout. So the original failure — a stale Jarvis env var blocking all voice — simply cannot happen anymore.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/65ce301a-8d65-4729-b4c3-390d9470cdc0.mp3','SUMMARY',38,'message','am_echo','2026-06-08T13:43:12.372Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('20e34fd2-4b46-4bc1-8eb4-d6b26f39c536','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Perfect — unified everything on My List, like you said: the menu, the page heading, and the URL all read My List now. So: Offers is a clean centered placeholder on the homepage, My List is a centered placeholder at slash-my-list, the search page moved to slash-compare and still works fully, and the top menu reads Offers, Compare, My List. Building and deploying now, then I''ll verify each route in real Chrome.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/20e34fd2-4b46-4bc1-8eb4-d6b26f39c536.mp3','MY LIST — UNIFIED',21,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T13:45:07.769Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('d2abb49e-9b59-453e-9ed5-c5d7aaf5b5ac','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Found it, and it was actually two problems stacked on top of each other — both confirmed straight from the gateway logs, not guessed. First, Gemma was getting killed by our forty-five second timeout. I gave it a ninety-second leash. But that only exposed the real problem: even with more time, Gemma came back empty, zero items. The logs showed why — it''s a reasoning model, and it burned its entire token budget thinking before it ever got to writing the answer. It literally ran out of room mid-thought. So I doubled its token budget. Now it works — same letter, Gemma returns six items, even one more than Mistral, and the logs show it finished with headroom to spare. Both fixes are per-model, so Mistral stays fast and tight. On your other question — the two boxes — there''s nothing broken there. It''s two boxes because the four-box experiment simply isn''t built yet. That''s the Phase One we designed. So if you''re happy with how Gemma''s behaving now, just say go and I''ll build the four boxes.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/d2abb49e-9b59-453e-9ed5-c5d7aaf5b5ac.mp3','FAMILY OS — GEMMA FIXED',49,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-08T13:45:16.912Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('3c38fab4-8a4c-4e51-9a42-1b4a7cd2d95e','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Quick one — the ringo command itself is fine. We added the ringo function to your zshrc last session, and it''s right there. The reason your terminal says command not found is that this terminal was already open before we added it, so it never loaded the new function. Just reload it and ringo will work.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/3c38fab4-8a4c-4e51-9a42-1b4a7cd2d95e.mp3','NATIVE — ringo not found',16,'message','am_echo','2026-06-08T13:45:51.921Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f39a5b43-a768-4af2-ac03-ee4f5633ced8','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Cheap. Cloudflare''s own log says Gemma''s read of that letter cost about seventeen hundredths of a cent — call it a fifth of a cent, or point one seven cents. That''s roughly six thousand three hundred tokens total, and almost all of it is Gemma''s reasoning on the output side. For comparison, Mistral read the exact same letter for under half that, about seven hundredths of a cent, because it doesn''t burn tokens thinking. So in plain terms, a dollar buys you around five or six hundred Gemma scans like this one. One caveat — that was a typed letter, not a real photo, so an actual photo would add a bit on the input side, but the reasoning is what dominates the cost.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f39a5b43-a768-4af2-ac03-ee4f5633ced8.mp3','FAMILY OS — GEMMA COST',34,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-08T13:47:49.279Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f8e6aff5-e0d5-4e82-bedf-eae4f85cd23a','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Looking at that settings warning now. Your Claude Code settings file has a permission rule that a recent update stopped accepting, so it''s just skipping that one line and loading the rest. Let me read the file and see exactly what''s there before I touch it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f8e6aff5-e0d5-4e82-bedf-eae4f85cd23a.mp3','SETTINGS WARNING',13,'message','am_echo','2026-06-08T13:49:47.184Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('adabacbe-c995-4a26-a8c7-0a58a2c54c04','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Fixed and verified. The bad rule is gone, replaced with five valid per-server rules — one each for Gmail, Calendar, Drive, the Jarvis dashboard, and Context7. The JSON parses clean. The warning won''t come back on your next session, and those MCP tools still run without prompting you. The only catch: if you connect a brand-new MCP server later, you''ll need to add a line for it too, because the new rules killed the blanket all-MCP allow.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/adabacbe-c995-4a26-a8c7-0a58a2c54c04.mp3','SETTINGS FIXED',23,'message','am_echo','2026-06-08T13:50:45.194Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7ddf1594-af1e-4ab5-bcc5-9341e80048df','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','All done and verified live. Recap: Offers — your homepage — is now a single centered word, no template. My List is a centered placeholder at slash-my-list. The two Dutch routes are English now: vergelijken became compare, mandje became my-list. The top menu reads Offers, Compare, My List, and the compare search still works and still shows every result. I checked all three in real Chrome and took a screenshot — it''s clean, the green Offers centered between the nav and footer. Committed. Two honest notes. The footer still has a small Over column with two Dutch links to pages that don''t exist yet — out of scope, I left them. And the old vergelijken URL will keep showing its old cached page for a few hours until Cloudflare''s edge cache expires; nothing links to it so it''s harmless, but if you want the old URLs to redirect cleanly to the new ones I can add that in one line. What''s next?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7ddf1594-af1e-4ab5-bcc5-9341e80048df.mp3','ROUTES + PLACEHOLDERS DONE',43,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T13:51:03.514Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('1db8e442-8ce0-4031-b2df-f004d5931a84','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Here''s the whole landscape as two tables. The first is the short list — the options actually worth using for your docs, with my picks marked. The second is everything else we looked at, mostly tools to skip and why. Read it down the editable-text and HTML-embed columns — those two are what protect your way of working. Bottom line at the end: tune the Mermaid you already have, let me write the syntax for you day to day, and keep D2 in your back pocket for when one diagram really needs to shine.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/1db8e442-8ce0-4031-b2df-f004d5931a84.mp3','OPTIONS TABLE',29,'message','bm_george','2026-06-08T13:51:31.787Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('ecc773eb-1215-43d5-af03-ed1ab1a02eaf','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Crystal clear — the URLs stay English, all the visible text goes Dutch. That''s actually our standing convention anyway: English routes, Dutch on the page. So I''m flipping the labels back: the menu becomes Aanbiedingen, Vergelijken, Mijn lijst; the two placeholders read Aanbiedingen and Mijn lijst; the page titles go Dutch too. The compare and my-list URLs don''t change. The compare search page was already Dutch, so that stays as-is. Rebuilding and verifying now. One small call: I''m translating My List as Mijn lijst — if you''d prefer Boodschappenlijst or Mijn lijstje, just say so and I''ll swap it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/ecc773eb-1215-43d5-af03-ed1ab1a02eaf.mp3','TEXT TO DUTCH, URLS STAY',31,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T13:54:27.316Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('b2c0dca6-ea26-4547-81be-cef90a39c2e8','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Done and verified. The visible text is Dutch now, and the URLs stayed English exactly like you said. The menu reads Aanbiedingen, Vergelijken, Mijn lijst; the two placeholders say Aanbiedingen and Mijn lijst; but the addresses are still slash-compare and slash-my-list. I checked it in real Chrome — all correct — and committed. I''ve also locked this in as the rule for this project going forward: on the deployed site the routes stay English, and everything a visitor reads is Dutch. What''s next?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/b2c0dca6-ea26-4547-81be-cef90a39c2e8.mp3','DUTCH TEXT LIVE',25,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T13:56:07.778Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('4edecfd0-be45-459a-8558-2451e1767799','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Found it, and I just confirmed it live rather than trusting the old note. The dashboard front-end is healthy and Cloudflare Access is working — the problem is the database. I pulled the live connection string and queried Neon directly, and it still answers with ''data transfer quota exceeded''. So it''s the same thing we caught on June fifth: the free tier blew its five-gigabyte monthly egress cap and went into a hard 402 block, which makes every API call fail behind your login. The fix that stops it recurring is already deployed — the tickets page was polling every five seconds and burning through the quota — but that can''t refund the bytes already spent this period. So it stays down until either Neon''s monthly quota resets, or you upgrade the plan for an instant restore. That''s the call I left for you, since it costs money. Tell me which way you want and I''ll handle it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/4edecfd0-be45-459a-8558-2451e1767799.mp3','DASHBOARD DOWN — NEON 402',44,'message','am_echo','2026-06-08T14:05:58.765Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('a424dd9d-c639-48e0-a538-13a5a7afdb4d','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','The four-page structure is live and verified. Home is now the first page with a search box, Offers moved to its own page, and the menu reads Home, Aanbiedingen, Vergelijken, Mijn lijst. Now the real decision, and it''s yours. You asked the home search to cover the whole catalog. Right now it searches the roughly nine thousand products we match across chains — but the full catalog is sixty-three thousand, and the other fifty-one thousand are single-chain products, including most fresh produce like apples. Searching all of them is exactly what closes the appel-only-shows-juice gap — but it reverses the scope decision we locked earlier today, it''s a seven-times-bigger search index, and those single-chain products have no comparison page to land on, so I''d show their price and cheapest store inline instead. My recommendation is to go full catalog — that''s what makes Home meaningfully different from Compare and matches what you asked. But it''s your call, so I''ve put the two options on screen.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/a424dd9d-c639-48e0-a538-13a5a7afdb4d.mp3','HOME SEARCH SCOPE',49,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T14:07:14.414Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7d86987e-a5fc-4548-8c41-cf0a5f6c226c','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','It''s live — go look. Every capture now gives you four boxes: Gemma and Mistral, each run two ways — code-built, where the model just reads and our code builds the events, reminders and to-dos, and model-built, where the model builds them itself. All four answer now. I had to give Gemma a much longer leash for its model-built box, because structuring is heavier work and it was timing out — so that one box runs slower, around a minute, and honestly that slowness is itself a finding about Gemma. Every box opens to its full fan-out so you can compare all four before you pick one. I also ran Forge over the new code, and it earned its keep — it caught a real isolation bug where one malformed reading would have crashed all four boxes at once, plus a cap that was silently hiding events, a five-event letter was only showing two. Both fixed. And the experiment is already paying off on the very first letter: Gemma got the year right, twenty twenty-six, while Mistral resolved the same dates to twenty twenty-five — that''s the year bug we talked about, and now you can see exactly which model handles it. I left the tab open on your screen with a test capture. Throw your own letters at it, and once you''ve seen enough to pick a winner, we wire up Phase two and make it save for real.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7d86987e-a5fc-4548-8c41-cf0a5f6c226c.mp3','FAMILY OS — 4 BOXES LIVE',62,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-08T14:12:28.115Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('e8d8509c-5d6a-41d7-b1c0-586985bec317','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','One important catch before I build. I grounded this in the live code, not the old notes. Moving the 135 megabytes of voice audio out of Postgres means reading it out — and reading is exactly the egress that''s blocked at 402 right now — so that step physically can''t run until the database is unblocked. And none of the hardening actually brings the dashboard back; it stays down until the DB is back. What hardening does is stop it re-blowing the cap the moment it returns. So I''m doing the part that''s executable today: there are about thirteen list endpoints running unbounded queries with no limit — including your sessions table with fourteen hundred rows — and that''s the biggest recurring drain. I''m bringing in Forge to add sane limits across all of them now, then I''ll verify the build. The voice-to-R2 move and the actual restore both wait on your upgrade-or-wait call.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/e8d8509c-5d6a-41d7-b1c0-586985bec317.mp3','HARDENING — SCOPE',46,'message','am_echo','2026-06-08T14:38:07.606Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f26b5143-c695-4649-9a25-bc1c229375ad','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Full catalog it is — building the all-catalog search now. I''ll write a new read-only query over all sixty-three thousand products, build a trimmed search index, wire it into the home page with single-chain results showing price and store inline while cross-chain ones still link to the comparison page, then have Forge run a cross-vendor audit on the firewall before I call it done.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f26b5143-c695-4649-9a25-bc1c229375ad.mp3','BUILDING FULL-CATALOG SEARCH',19,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T14:40:10.701Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('b9f22848-3cd5-45ee-8cd4-1f837da2e067','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Got it, and it''s a smart move — bank every output with its full manufacturing info so over two weeks you''ve got real data to judge from, not a gut feel. I''ll make the app automatically log all four outputs of every capture — yours or Tamar''s, photo or text — into a table, with who submitted it, the model, the method, the latency, and the full events, reminders and to-dos. Then a Log page that shows the whole pile, expandable, with an export. Let me wire it in.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/b9f22848-3cd5-45ee-8cd4-1f837da2e067.mp3','FAMILY OS — OUTPUT LOG',24,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-08T14:44:18.947Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('e541aff4-a612-4040-80c0-0fd217bfbbc8','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','All saved. The full options table is now a reference doc in Downloads, and I''ve put two notes in your memory so a fresh session starts clean: one on the diagram approach — refined Mermaid plus ELK as your standard, let AI write the syntax, D2 for the ceiling — and one on Interceptor, now on the new version with screenshots fixed. The one thing still on your plate for next time: reload the Interceptor extension in Chrome when you get a moment — the exact steps are in that memory note. Everything else is backed up and recorded. Good session.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/e541aff4-a612-4040-80c0-0fd217bfbbc8.mp3','SAVED',34,'message','bm_george','2026-06-08T14:45:53.094Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('95ca1fcf-cb38-4c2e-9454-67b64a01fd72','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Hardening''s done and committed, and the full gate is green — typecheck, lint, and build all pass. I capped the twelve unbounded endpoints, and I also fixed the voice feed — it was polling every five seconds even on a hidden tab, the same pattern that blew the cap, which the June fifth fix had left alone. I held off deploying for two reasons: the deploy method is ambiguous and I won''t push blind, and there''s nothing to verify against until the database is back anyway. The honest bottom line: the dashboard stays down until you decide. Moving the voice audio out and the actual restore both need the database unblocked. So it comes down to two choices — upgrade Neon''s plan for about nineteen euros a month and it''s back in minutes, which is my lean since it''s cheap and the recurrence is now fixed, or wait for the free monthly reset at no cost but stay down until then. Tell me which and I''ll take it from there.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/95ca1fcf-cb38-4c2e-9454-67b64a01fd72.mp3','HARDENING DONE — YOUR CALL',45,'message','am_echo','2026-06-08T14:46:15.727Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('30ad5851-26af-444c-9381-047d0d3b9bd7','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Forge audit done. Codex at high reasoning plus my own cross-check against the schema landed on a FAIL verdict, but it''s a soft fail — two things actually need fixing before ship. First, the home search can show a product as being in multiple stores yet give it no comparison-page link, because the slug map and the chain counter run through two different filter pipelines. That''s the real bug. Second, the single-chain store link passes the database URL through HTML-escaping but never checks the scheme, so a javascript-colon URL would not be neutralized — defense-in-depth, low real-world likelihood since the URL comes from a trusted column, but the audit''s XSS requirement isn''t fully met. Good news: I independently confirmed the firewall holds — the new SQL is provably select-only — and I knocked down codex''s chain-count concern, because the schema makes chain code and chain id strictly one-to-one. Two genuine fixes, three nits, one noted perf tradeoff.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/30ad5851-26af-444c-9381-047d0d3b9bd7.mp3','FORGE AUDIT',52,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T14:49:37.817Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('046f39d6-5d4b-4d0d-be3f-34ca5b16866a','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Done and live. The home page now searches the whole food catalog — forty-two thousand seven hundred products. The proof: searching appel now returns fourteen hundred results including real fresh apples, so the gap we''d accepted is closed. Single-chain products that have no comparison page show their price and cheapest store inline, while cross-chain ones still link into the comparison. The data is about two megabytes compressed, lazy-loaded only when you start typing, so it stays fast. I recorded the scope reversal in the design doc and the build registry and committed everything. Forge is still running its cross-vendor audit on the new database query in the background — I''ll tell you what it finds the moment it''s back.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/046f39d6-5d4b-4d0d-be3f-34ca5b16866a.mp3','FULL-CATALOG SEARCH LIVE',36,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T14:49:53.752Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('64d44f14-dfa4-41df-9d39-96484cbb67a6','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Forge earned its keep — it found a real one, not a hallucination. The home index counted a product''s chains from raw data, but the comparison pages count them after filtering out bad prices, so the two could disagree — a product could say three stores on home while its comparison page shows two. I''m fixing it by building the cross-chain home entries from the exact same snapshot the product pages use, so they can''t diverge. It also flagged that the single-chain store links weren''t scheme-checked — defense in depth — so I''m allowlisting http links only. Two quick fixes plus a couple of nits, then I rebuild, redeploy, re-verify, and update the audit record.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/64d44f14-dfa4-41df-9d39-96484cbb67a6.mp3','FORGE FOUND A BUG — FIXING',34,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T14:52:40.518Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('ff3c3514-094e-47be-b519-83c403fb6458','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Done — the output log is live, go look at the new Log tab. From now on, every capture automatically banks all four of its outputs, no matter who submits it or whether it''s a photo or text. It records the whole story: who sent it, the input, the model, the method, the latency, the token count, and the full events, reminders and to-dos. The Log page shows the entire pile as a table — one section per capture, every output expandable, and an Export button so you can pull the raw data whenever you want. I verified it end to end: a test capture wrote all four rows, and the manufacturing signal is already there — Gemma burns over five thousand tokens reasoning while Mistral does it in under three hundred. One thing I want to flag honestly: every capture now takes about seventy seconds or more, because it waits for Gemma''s model-built box, which is the slow one. That''s the price of keeping Gemma in the race. After a couple weeks of real data, the log will tell you whether Gemma''s model-built method actually earns that slot — and if it doesn''t, dropping it makes every capture fast again. So now you just use it normally for two weeks, and the evidence piles up on its own.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/ff3c3514-094e-47be-b519-83c403fb6458.mp3','FAMILY OS — LOG LIVE',60,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-08T14:55:07.844Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('720ed9cb-eba6-47dc-a9c9-29f480e7289f','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','All done, and Forge made it better. It found a real bug — the home page could show a different store count than the comparison page for the same product, because the two were computed from different snapshots. I fixed it so the cross-chain home results now come from the exact same data the comparison pages use, and I verified zero mismatches across all nine thousand of them. I also locked the single-chain store links down to http-only, like it suggested. Redeployed and re-checked live: appel still returns fourteen hundred results, everything consistent. It''s committed, the audit''s recorded in the build doc, and the cross-vendor check is genuinely back in the loop. That''s the full-catalog home search done and verified end to end.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/720ed9cb-eba6-47dc-a9c9-29f480e7289f.mp3','FULL-CATALOG SEARCH — DONE + AUDITED',38,'message','af_nova','2026-06-08T14:56:09.062Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('61e362f1-74d7-4d7b-a732-81b2b8be9db7','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','All saved, you''re good to start a new session. Everything''s committed — the working tree is clean, the last four commits are today''s Family OS work. I''ve written up the whole session in memory, and I moved Family OS to the top of your resume pointer, so a fresh session will land right here: the two-by-two experiment is live, the output log is banking every capture, and the one decision waiting for you is whether Gemma''s slow model-built method is worth the latency — which the log itself will answer after a couple of weeks of real use. I also cleaned up the stray screenshots and stopped the background watchdog. Nothing''s left hanging. Talk to you in the next one.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/61e362f1-74d7-4d7b-a732-81b2b8be9db7.mp3','FAMILY OS — SESSION SAVED',35,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T06:31:41.746Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('9fa4f1e1-714d-4c22-9723-bd9bb59650d7','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','All saved — you''re good to start a new session. I wrote one memory capturing that Ringo is now the default agent, where agent identity actually resolves across all its fallback owners, and which leftover Jarvis references are intentional so a future session doesn''t undo them. The work ISA is closed and the audit is recorded inside it. There''s no git repo under dot-claude, so every edit is already persisted straight to disk — nothing pending, nothing to commit. A fresh session will load all of this automatically. Talk soon as Ringo.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/9fa4f1e1-714d-4c22-9723-bd9bb59650d7.mp3','SESSION SAVE',28,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T06:33:15.669Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('27fa0207-2021-4a05-a648-fef126fc27d7','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','All saved — you''re clear to start fresh. The repo is clean and fully committed, and everything from today is live on the site. I updated the resume pointer and the NL-Supermarkets memory so the next session picks up exactly where we are: the four-page app, the full-catalog home search, the Forge fixes, and the codex re-auth are all recorded, with the next launch steps spelled out — SEO plumbing, affiliate links, the trust layer, and picking the real brand and domain. I reconciled the resume note with the parallel Family-OS session so nothing got clobbered. Good session — see you in the next one.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/27fa0207-2021-4a05-a648-fef126fc27d7.mp3','SESSION SAVED',29,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T06:37:44.650Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('2fcb8f43-f0f7-43c8-bd14-d2d3d3487f01','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','I read your doctor output. Good news first: there''s no real problem. The whole thing is green except for two yellow advisories, and both are harmless. The first is your My Jarvis Dashboard MCP server saying it needs authentication — that''s the same dashboard connector we already know isn''t provisioned on this account, so it''s expected, not new. The second isn''t an error at all, it''s a heads-up that you have so many skills installed that Claude Code is abbreviating some of their descriptions to save context. Everything else — updates, remote control, search, your install — is healthy. You just updated to two-one-six-nine. Nothing here needs fixing.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/2fcb8f43-f0f7-43c8-bd14-d2d3d3487f01.mp3','NATIVE: /doctor readout',34,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T06:38:16.194Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('a0f2880e-de0e-4106-a79e-cf2e966b86a4','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Here''s the twist — there''s nothing local to delete. The My Jarvis Dashboard isn''t a real MCP server on your machine; it''s a claude-dot-ai connector that syncs down from your account. Your local config only has two leftover references to it: a cached ''ever connected'' entry and a permission pre-approval. I''m cleaning both of those now. But the actual connector lives in your claude-dot-ai account settings, so to make it truly gone for good I either need to drive your browser to the connectors page and remove it, or you remove it there yourself. Otherwise it just re-syncs and comes back next session. I''ve backed up your config first.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/a0f2880e-de0e-4106-a79e-cf2e966b86a4.mp3','ALGORITHM: delete Jarvis MCP',34,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T06:42:06.143Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('179127fc-d150-4627-8416-78898713e19f','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Local side is done and verified — both config files are still valid, and every reference to the dashboard is gone. One thing left, and it''s the one that actually matters: the connector itself lives in your claude-dot-ai account. Go to claude-dot-ai, Settings, then Connectors, and remove My Jarvis Dashboard there. That''s one click and it''s permanent. If you''d rather I drive your browser and do it for you, just say so — but honestly it''s faster if you click it yourself.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/179127fc-d150-4627-8416-78898713e19f.mp3','ALGORITHM: Jarvis MCP cleanup done',22,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T06:43:05.250Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('5582c4a3-65cd-4b60-988c-ead1f99c3165','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Doing it now. I''m opening Chrome to your claude-dot-ai connector settings through Interceptor, finding the My Jarvis Dashboard connector, and removing it. Give me a moment to drive the browser.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/5582c4a3-65cd-4b60-988c-ead1f99c3165.mp3','Interceptor: remove Jarvis connector',11,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T06:43:30.972Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f717712c-e379-4f73-ba89-21ba0b58a64f','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Okay Yaron, I''m caught up on NL Supermarkets. The consumer app, Scherp, is live and solid. The full-catalog home search shipped and passed the Forge audit, so the data spine, the cross-chain comparison, the nine thousand product pages, and the search are all done and verified. But here''s the thing that matters most: none of it is visible to Google yet. The whole site is sitting behind a noindex placeholder on the pages-dot-dev domain, which means the SEO clock, the entire point of Phase One, hasn''t started. And it can''t start until you pick a brand name and register a real domain. That''s the gate, and it''s your call, not something I can build. What I can do right now in parallel is knock out the three remaining launch blockers: the affiliate deep-links so we earn from day one, the trust layer, and the SEO infrastructure. My recommendation is I start on those while you think about the name. But tell me where you want to aim this session.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f717712c-e379-4f73-ba89-21ba0b58a64f.mp3','NL-SUPER · RESUME',45,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T06:47:42.597Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('b59bd18a-f3eb-430d-8875-62196572fefb','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','All saved. I wrote two things to memory: the dashboard state — that it''s still down, the hardening is committed but not deployed, and the upgrade-versus-wait decision is the open hook to resume from — and a new reference note on that Claude Code permission-rule change so it won''t surprise us again. You''re clear to start fresh; just clear the conversation or open a new Claude. When you come back, say ''the dashboard'' and the whole thread reconstructs from memory. The upgrade-or-wait call is still yours whenever you want to make it — nothing else on the dashboard moves until then.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/b59bd18a-f3eb-430d-8875-62196572fefb.mp3','MEMORY SAVED — CLEAR TO RESET',28,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T06:48:43.269Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('e6fbe6e3-2484-4abc-ad22-5041e9268c3c','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Entering the Algorithm. Yaron picked Phase Two, so I''m building the deals digest, the recurring-visit engine. First I''m grounding myself: reading the existing Scherp app structure, the promo decoder module we already built and tested over twenty-one thousand live deals, and the seam contract that says which database views I''m allowed to read. Then I''ll scaffold the criteria and plan the build.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/e6fbe6e3-2484-4abc-ad22-5041e9268c3c.mp3','ALGORITHM · OBSERVE',20,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T06:50:58.936Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('9596f4df-c0ed-4e4b-90f2-719421fa6f56','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','It''s gone. I drove Chrome to your claude-dot-ai connector settings, selected the My Jarvis Dashboard custom connector, opened its menu, hit Remove, and confirmed. I verified the list afterward — it now shows only GitHub, Gmail, Calendar and Drive. No more Jarvis. That''s the real deletion at the source, so it won''t re-sync back. I''d already cleaned the two local leftovers in your config, and I backed that up first. I also closed the browser tab I opened and tidied up the screenshots I took. Next time you run doctor, that MCP warning will be gone.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/9596f4df-c0ed-4e4b-90f2-719421fa6f56.mp3','Interceptor: Jarvis connector removed',30,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T06:51:04.793Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('29489b15-7353-47fa-91b9-90519f3e8a04','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Okay, I''m oriented on Family OS. The sim app is live and healthy — Gemma and Mistral both reading, persistence and auth all up. I checked the banked experiment data: only about two real test captures so far, so it''s too early to crown a winning model, but two things are already clear. Gemma''s model-built path is the latency anchor at fifty-one seconds, and Gemma gets bare dates to the right year while Mistral lands on last year — that''s the year-resolution bug. The biggest open thread is Slice four: real Google Calendar sync and reminders, the step that makes events actually leave the app and land on your and Tamar''s phones. My recommendation is to fold the cheap year-fix into that and make calendar sync the headline — but since that means wiring OAuth against your real Google accounts, I want you to pick the thread before I open it up. I''ve put the options on screen.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/29489b15-7353-47fa-91b9-90519f3e8a04.mp3','FAMILY_OS · ORIENT',50,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T06:52:38.827Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('2d42545d-d581-40d0-a16e-bbf9ff115b3a','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Found it. That four-thirty a.m. Telegram was the NL-Supermarkets scraper checking in after its scheduled run. The pipeline runs automatically every Tuesday and Friday at four a.m. on the Hetzner box — today is Tuesday, so it fired at four, finished around four thirty-three, and sent you the alert right then. That''s the why-four-a.m.: it''s a fixed cron-style schedule, not a random event. Two issues it flagged. First, Dekamarkt crashed — its GraphQL gateway rejected the request after one second and pulled zero products, so that scraper is broken and needs a fix. Second, Hoogvliet shrank — it came back with seven thousand seven hundred products versus a baseline of ten and a half thousand, a twenty-six percent drop, which usually means a partial scrape rather than a real catalog change. The other six chains were all green. Nothing is on fire and your data is mostly intact, but Dekamarkt is fully down and Hoogvliet looks suspicious. Want me to dig into both and get them fixed?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/2d42545d-d581-40d0-a16e-bbf9ff115b3a.mp3','NL-SUPER PIPELINE ALERT',52,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T06:54:50.370Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('88f8971a-3bd2-4f99-90ff-e1bd042b2dfc','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Entering the Think phase. The core design insight: about half of Dutch supermarket deals are multi-buy, like one-plus-one gratis or three-for-five-euro. A plain feed shows the single-item shelf price with no discount, which hides the real saving. Our tested decoder computes the true effective per-item price, so a one-plus-one becomes minus fifty percent effective, and ranks honestly against simple percent deals. That honest ranking is the moat. I''m now locking the digest shape: a lean shippable feed, category and chain facets, a validity countdown, and value-first sorting.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/88f8971a-3bd2-4f99-90ff-e1bd042b2dfc.mp3','ALGORITHM · THINK',30,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T06:56:47.350Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('e2593860-3613-453d-869b-bed33314887d','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Entering the Build phase. I''m reading the existing home-search island so the deals page mirrors the same pattern and the locked green-utility design, then I''ll extend the seam to emit the full deals feed with the decoder wired in.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/e2593860-3613-453d-869b-bed33314887d.mp3','ALGORITHM · BUILD',12,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T06:57:55.143Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('0cdfaea1-4eec-452c-905e-e117e550669c','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Entering the Algorithm. New thread: I''m going to map out when each Dutch supermarket chain actually refreshes the data on its website — the weekly promotion rotation and any nightly price refresh — so we can time the scraper to when the data really changes instead of guessing. Starting by reading what we already know and pulling each chain''s own API metadata, since their promotion validity windows tell us exactly when things flip.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/0cdfaea1-4eec-452c-905e-e117e550669c.mp3','ALGORITHM — ENTRY',22,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T06:58:57.856Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('2bc76cdc-3bed-446b-969c-ca732616451b','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Done — and the cadence map connects straight back to this morning''s alert. Here''s the picture. Each chain rolls its promo week on a fixed weekday, and they flip at midnight Amsterdam time. The big finding: three of your major chains — Dirk, Jumbo, and Hoogvliet — all start their new week on Wednesday, running Wednesday through Tuesday. Albert Heijn and Aldi roll on Monday. DekaMarkt rolls Tuesday. Vomar runs Sunday to Saturday. Spar is the messy one — it''s a franchise with a roughly two-week national folder, so treat it as uncertain. Now the kicker: your scraper runs Tuesday and Friday. That means for Dirk, Jumbo and Hoogvliet you''re scraping Tuesday — the dying last day of their old week — and never scraping Wednesday, when the fresh week actually lands. That''s almost certainly why Hoogvliet showed up minus twenty-six percent this morning: a Tuesday scrape catches the catalog as the week empties out, not a real data loss. None of the chains publish an exact refresh clock-time, but the whole Dutch price-comparison ecosystem re-pulls nightly, which is why your four a.m. window is actually well chosen. My recommendation: move the Tuesday run to Wednesday, or better, go Monday-Wednesday-Friday — Monday catches AH and Aldi fresh, Wednesday catches the three Wednesday chains fresh, Friday stays as an integrity check. The box is idle and cheap, so three runs a week costs almost nothing. I haven''t touched the schedule — that''s your call. Want me to make the change?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/2bc76cdc-3bed-446b-969c-ca732616451b.mp3','CADENCE MAP — RESULT',76,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T07:06:22.163Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('998551ca-f27e-4e5f-a402-da50bb34fb96','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','The year-resolution bug is fixed and live. I reproduced it first — a bare ''third of March'' with no year, today being June ninth, came back from Mistral as March third of this year, which is three months in the past. That''s the bug: the model resolves the day and month but guesses the year, and guesses wrong. The fix is one deterministic function on the server — when the source text states no explicit year, I re-resolve the date to the nearest future occurrence off the server''s own clock. It''s idempotent, so dates the model already got right are left untouched and unflagged, and it also corrects the to-do deadlines. Crucially, I gated it on real textual evidence — an actual year in the source — never on the model''s own self-label, because Mistral mislabels these, which is exactly the safety-gate lesson from the auto-save audit. I verified three cases live: the bug repro now lands on twenty twenty-seven across all four readings, ''next Tuesday'' stays unchanged, and an explicitly-written twenty twenty-five date is preserved even though it''s in the past. Committed, ISA updated, test rows cleaned up. The natural next step is Slice four — real Google Calendar sync — and the year-fix is now a done precursor so we won''t push wrong-year events to your real calendars. I can also run a Forge cross-vendor audit on this if you want the extra pass. Your call.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/998551ca-f27e-4e5f-a402-da50bb34fb96.mp3','FAMILY_OS · YEAR-FIX DONE',81,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T07:06:47.856Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('39bdae09-8520-48a7-8abe-ddc1ac905538','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Entering the Verify phase. The deal feed, the decoder integration, the page, and the build all passed, and the deploy just landed live. Now I''m verifying the production offers page with a real browser, then I''ll run the Forge cross-vendor audit and an advisor check before calling it done.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/39bdae09-8520-48a7-8abe-ddc1ac905538.mp3','ALGORITHM · VERIFY',16,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T07:08:38.461Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('488070e8-4c93-4344-94a0-7a8fd34e2444','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','On it — moving the supermarket scrape to Monday, Wednesday, Friday at four a.m., and shifting the watchdog to match so it doesn''t false-alarm on the days we no longer run. Reading the current timer files first, then applying.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/488070e8-4c93-4344-94a0-7a8fd34e2444.mp3','EXECUTE — RESCHEDULE',12,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T07:08:58.504Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('16fce47d-ac75-44c6-a8d1-59cd041e2f1d','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Done. The supermarket scraper now runs Monday, Wednesday, and Friday at four a.m., and the watchdog moves with it on the same days so it won''t false-alarm. Both timers are live and verified on the box. The next run is tomorrow, Wednesday at four — which is exactly when Dirk, Jumbo and Hoogvliet roll their new promo week, so it should pull the fresh full catalog and, as a side benefit, tell us whether yesterday''s Hoogvliet shrink was just the end-of-week effect we suspected. I also updated the box runbook so the schedule on record matches what''s actually running. The dekamarkt crash is still open whenever you want to tackle it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/16fce47d-ac75-44c6-a8d1-59cd041e2f1d.mp3','RESCHEDULE — DONE',33,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T07:10:01.647Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('00a17a5d-496d-4287-ab04-ae7ac1d09111','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Understood — skipping Forge. The year-fix is fully shipped and banked: code and ISA committed, deployed, verified live, memory updated. Nothing left hanging on it. Whenever you''re ready, the next real step is Slice four — Google Calendar sync — but that one needs you in the loop because it wires OAuth against your and Tamar''s actual Google accounts, so just say the word and I''ll scope it with you first. Or we leave it here for now.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/00a17a5d-496d-4287-ab04-ae7ac1d09111.mp3','FAMILY_OS · NOTED',24,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T07:10:36.795Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('957f9808-84d4-4066-b899-ffb4780af653','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Yes — done, and it''s possible exactly the way you wanted. I decoupled the alert from the scrape. The four a.m. run no longer messages you the moment it finishes; instead it writes its result to a file, and a new reporter job delivers the Telegram at eight a.m. sharp. So even a hard crash at four just waits quietly in the file until eight. It only pings you when there''s actually a problem — healthy runs stay silent. I tested both halves live on the box: I pushed a fake alert through the real eight-o''clock job and you should have gotten a test message, and I ran a real scrape to confirm it now saves instead of sending. The schedule on the box is now a clean sequence: scrape at four, deliver at eight, and the watchdog at nine still catches the rare case where a run doesn''t happen at all. Next real delivery is tomorrow, Wednesday, at eight. The only thing still open is the DekaMarkt crash whenever you want it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/957f9808-84d4-4066-b899-ffb4780af653.mp3','08:00 DELIVERY — DONE',47,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T07:19:24.507Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('8686beff-f1b2-47c7-82e5-d2913822ebe1','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Entering the Learn phase. Phase Two is live: the deals digest is shipped, decoded, and verified on production. The big lesson this run — unit tests on a pure function don''t guarantee honesty at the feed layer. Forge''s cross-vendor audit caught four real ways the feed could show a fabricated discount that my own checks missed, and the fix was to make the real price delta the single ground truth. All four are now zero-instance. Writing the build docs and updating memory.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/8686beff-f1b2-47c7-82e5-d2913822ebe1.mp3','ALGORITHM · LEARN',25,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T07:22:38.081Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('d7f8fa87-cf29-47c5-9c13-d2b1cc8a2645','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Alright Yaron, Rex here. So you want a meeting capture tool — punch in a Google Meet or Zoom meeting ID and have it record and pull out everything that was said. Good idea, but there''s a real catch I need to flag before we design anything: you can''t just hand a meeting ID to a script and have it silently record. Both platforms gate that hard, and there are consent laws on top. There are a few legitimate ways through this though. Let me load the Algorithm and lay out the real options for how this can actually work.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/d7f8fa87-cf29-47c5-9c13-d2b1cc8a2645.mp3','REX — Meeting Capture',26,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:24:25.900Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('878ac8e8-1001-4dd4-a037-2dbca8cc80ca','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Phase Two is done and live, Yaron. The deals digest is shipped at slash offers on the Scherp app: six and a half thousand food deals, food-first, with the promo decoder doing the real work — over a thousand multi-buy deals now show their true per-unit price, so a one-plus-one reads as effectively half price and a four-for-two-fifty reads as sixty-three cents a piece, ranked honestly by real value, not by a fake headline percent. Category and chain filters, validity countdowns, all verified live in a real browser. The big win was the Forge cross-vendor audit: it found four ways the feed could quietly lie about a discount that my own checks missed, and they''re all fixed and re-audited to zero. The whole thing is committed, the build docs and memory are updated. The one gate still in your hands is picking a brand name and a domain — that''s what starts the SEO clock. Want me to take on the multi-buy radar next, or wire the deals feed into the box so it refreshes itself twice a week?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/878ac8e8-1001-4dd4-a037-2dbca8cc80ca.mp3','NL-SUPER · PHASE 2 DONE',49,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T07:25:40.635Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('e0d0a8bf-bfe3-49de-a401-0114ffe7438b','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Okay Yaron, I dug into all of it and here''s the hard truth up front: there is no way, on Zoom or Google Meet, to just type in a meeting ID and have something quietly record it. Both platforms lock recording to either owning the account or the host explicitly letting your app in. A meeting ID by itself authorizes nothing — that''s not something we can code around, it''s the design. So the real question isn''t how do we record by ID, it''s whose meetings are these. That single answer picks the entire architecture. If these are meetings you''re personally sitting in, the cleanest path by far is to capture the audio right off your own Mac and run it through the Whisper transcription you already have in pai-tools — no accounts, no approvals, no cost, fully private, and it works for Zoom, Meet, anything. That''s the ninety-percent win and we could have it running this week. If you actually need to capture meetings you''re not in — send a notetaker to a call you can''t attend — then it''s a real bot that joins as a visible participant: either Recall A-I at fifty cents an hour which works today, or self-hosting Vexa if you want every byte staying on your own infrastructure. So tell me which one you''re really after, and I''ll spec the build. My gut says we start with local capture, because it leans on what you already own.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/e0d0a8bf-bfe3-49de-a401-0114ffe7438b.mp3','REX — Meeting Capture',63,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:30:05.335Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('41b4df08-93e2-49d1-9fcf-9906a57b206c','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','All saved — you''re clear to start a fresh session. I kept four things: a new reference memory with the per-chain promo-rollover map, the box memory updated to the new Monday-Wednesday-Friday schedule plus the eight a.m. reporter, the NL-Supermarkets project memory updated with today''s two changes, and the index pointer so a new session finds it. The one open thread waiting for you next time is the DekaMarkt scraper crash — everything else from today is done and verified. Go ahead and start the new session whenever you like.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/41b4df08-93e2-49d1-9fcf-9906a57b206c.mp3','MEMORY SAVED — SESSION CLOSE',28,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T07:30:18.624Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('10978f82-6a02-4749-950e-a252ef129974','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Names are corrected on disk — Itamar, Iftach, Uri, Yoval. For the age and class, I need the real values from you — I won''t guess a kid''s age. I''ve got four, six, nine and eleven on file from your identity profile, but not which boy is which, so just map them for me — Itamar''s age, Iftach''s, and so on — and tell me the class for each in whatever format you want it shown, like Group six or Year five or just a number. One scope question: do you want Tamar''s five kids to get ages and classes too, or just your four for now? Give me those and I''ll add the fields, populate them, and ship it all in one deploy.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/10978f82-6a02-4749-950e-a252ef129974.mp3','FAMILY_OS · NEED AGE+CLASS',36,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T07:31:26.234Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7a5eee46-3799-4912-982e-00a2f4c80b78','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','One correction to what I just said: for the local path we should NOT use the cloud Whisper in pai-tools — that ships your audio off the Mac, so it wouldn''t actually be private, and it''d choke on an hour-long file anyway. We run Whisper locally instead, on-device. Same idea, but genuinely private and free. Details are on screen.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7a5eee46-3799-4912-982e-00a2f4c80b78.mp3','REX — correction',17,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:31:41.852Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('20704de1-0a48-41a0-97c9-491a78deee71','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Alright, building it. First thing I''m doing is checking what''s already on your Mac — whether BlackHole, ffmpeg, and a local Whisper are installed, what audio devices exist, and where your other pai CLIs live so this one matches the pattern. No point writing code against tools that aren''t there. At the same time I''m kicking off a design pass on the not-in-meeting bot solution so both tracks move together. Give me a minute to map the ground.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/20704de1-0a48-41a0-97c9-491a78deee71.mp3','REX — BUILD: env check',22,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:34:10.246Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('28d155ca-0952-4aec-b65d-b83c00bc310a','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Researching the send-a-notetaker-bot route for meetings you won''t attend. Verifying Recall dot AI and Vexa API specifics against official docs now, then I''ll deliver a build-ready spec with a recommendation tied to your stack.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/28d155ca-0952-4aec-b65d-b83c00bc310a.mp3','Ava Sterling — Meeting Bot Recon',13,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:36:17.061Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('07561794-d741-4843-bda7-ec06a97dc09f','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Done. The winner is Recall dot AI for the proof of concept, and here''s the strategic read: this is fundamentally a buy-versus-build decision where the thing you''d be building, headless Chrome that reliably joins and survives Zoom, Meet, and Teams meetings, is exactly the part with the worst cost-to-reliability ratio. Recall charges sixty-five cents an hour all-in and runs entirely from a Cloudflare Worker plus a webhook, no Hetzner box needed at all, because there''s no bot process you host. At five to twenty meetings a month you''re looking at one to fifteen euros, basically a rounding error against your capital. The self-host route, Vexa, is real and Apache licensed, but here''s the trap I want you to see three moves ahead: real-time Whisper needs a GPU, and your cx23 has none. On CPU the transcript drifts ninety seconds behind after one minute of talking. So the sovereign route isn''t a software install, it''s a GPU rental line item, and that completely changes the economics. My recommendation: ship Recall now as a thin pai-meet bot command, and only graduate to Vexa when either volume crosses roughly two hundred hours a month or a My Jarvis client demands data never leaves their infrastructure. Two hard caveats: the bot is a visible participant that must be admitted, so it can''t capture a meeting it has no link to, and under Dutch and G D P R rules a bot recording other people should announce itself. Full build ticket is in the terminal.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/07561794-d741-4843-bda7-ec06a97dc09f.mp3','Ava Sterling — Recommendation: Recall.ai',77,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:37:25.544Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('ec243c02-04ac-4e87-85d9-dd6fb06ef6d7','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Good catch on the images. Quick note first: the English text in your screenshot is just Chrome auto-translating the live Dutch page, not a bug. The missing pictures are real though. Before I touch anything, I''m checking where the image actually lives in the database — my hunch from the enrichment notes is that the deals view returns only the variant image, which is null for about half, while the product image is sitting right there unused. Diagnosing now.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/ec243c02-04ac-4e87-85d9-dd6fb06ef6d7.mp3','NL-SUPER · IMAGE FIX',21,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T07:41:17.784Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('d73267f4-c6cb-47d4-a03b-3b3bdaa7caf1','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Good call, and your instinct is right. First, straight answer: Recall A-I is not open source — it''s a closed commercial service, that''s the whole product. But yes, there are open-source equivalents we can self-host, which basically means running our OWN recall bot for free. The two strongest are Vexa and Attendee — both let a bot join a meeting by link and capture it. And here''s the key thing that kills the cost problem: the expensive part everyone worries about is GPU transcription, but we already have free local Whisper running on your Mac. So we let the open-source bot do the boring part — joining the call and grabbing the audio — and we run that audio through our own free Whisper afterward. No per-hour fee, no GPU rental. Let me verify the current state of these projects before I pick one, since you want this checked, not assumed.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/d73267f4-c6cb-47d4-a03b-3b3bdaa7caf1.mp3','REX — open-source recall',43,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:42:18.001Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7348d7e6-ccf1-486f-8e08-e62007477499','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Verified, here''s the verdict. Recall A-I is closed-source, confirmed — it''s out. The open-source equivalent we want is Attendee — MIT licensed, actively maintained, and it does exactly what Recall does: a bot joins a meeting by link and records it. The clever part: we run it in audio-only mode and skip its paid transcription completely, then pull the raw audio and run it through your own free local Whisper. It runs on your Hetzner box with no GPU. So the picture is now simple and clean: two front doors — your Mac for meetings you''re in, a self-hosted Attendee bot for meetings you''re not — both feeding one shared engine, free local Whisper plus a notes generator. I''m building that shared engine first since both tracks need it, and right now I''m proving the transcription works on a real audio clip so we''re on verified ground. Standing up Attendee on the box is the next move, on your word, since it touches your remote infrastructure.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7348d7e6-ccf1-486f-8e08-e62007477499.mp3','REX — verdict: Attendee + local Whisper',47,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:48:12.531Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('839939bd-9bdc-4498-bfac-c87ef0c4c58a','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Your four boys are done and live — I corrected the spellings to Iftach and Yoval, added the ages, and the classes: Itamar and Iftach in Year six, Uri in Year one, Yoval in Foundation slash one. I verified it in the real browser — all four cards render correctly. Now the Tamar part is the interesting one. You don''t want me hardcoding her kids, you want her to fill in her own family inside her area — and that''s a real shift. Right now the family roster is hardcoded in the app''s source. For Tamar to enter her own kids, the roster has to become editable, per-household data that lives in the database and is scoped to her login, so she only ever touches her own family. That''s a proper slice: a members table, a scoped create-edit-delete API just like events and to-dos, and an editable Family page where you add a child and set their name, age, class, colour. She already has her login and link from before, so there''s nothing to send — the missing piece is just the editing screen. It''s cross-cutting enough that I want your go before I build it. One choice: should I pre-fill her side with the five placeholder names I guessed earlier for her to correct, or leave it empty so she adds all five from scratch? Tell me that and whether to start, and I''m on it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/839939bd-9bdc-4498-bfac-c87ef0c4c58a.mp3','FAMILY_OS · TAMAR ROSTER PLAN',73,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T07:50:13.284Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('be83ada8-4c8e-486d-91a0-9d9eee5f79de','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Good — let''s prove the language support before anything else. English already transcribed perfectly. The model is the multilingual large-v3-turbo, so Hebrew should work too, but I''m testing it for real now with a Hebrew audio clip and automatic language detection, rather than taking it on faith. One sec.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/be83ada8-4c8e-486d-91a0-9d9eee5f79de.mp3','REX — Hebrew + English check',16,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:51:08.921Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('4eaa0cc8-e1d8-481f-ac31-d89d38117963','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Confirmed — both work perfectly. English transcribed exactly, and Hebrew came back letter-perfect, correct Hebrew script, and the model auto-detected Hebrew on its own at ninety-nine point five percent confidence with no manual setting. So the engine handles both languages and figures out which one it''s hearing automatically — exactly right for your mix of Hebrew and English meetings. One honest caveat: each test clip was a single language. Whisper locks onto one dominant language per recording, so a meeting that heavily switches back and forth mid-sentence between Hebrew and English might lose a little accuracy on the secondary language. But for meetings that are mostly one or the other, which is the normal case, it''s excellent. Bottom line: yes, Hebrew and English are both covered, automatically.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/4eaa0cc8-e1d8-481f-ac31-d89d38117963.mp3','REX — both languages confirmed',41,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T07:51:47.105Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('062bd372-ca70-42ef-a41c-ca442d0f65c6','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Okay, the whole thing in plain terms. Picture two front doors that open into the same room. The room is the engine we already proved works: take any meeting audio, run it through Whisper locally on your Mac to get a transcript, then have the AI turn that transcript into clean notes — summary, decisions, action items. Free, local, and we know it handles Hebrew and English. Everything else is just feeding audio into that room.
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7cddf567-cb2b-422a-a06c-9fefdac989cb','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Good question. Let me actually look at the Gmail CLI''s code rather than answer from memory, since whether it loads context each run is a real architectural detail worth verifying.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7cddf567-cb2b-422a-a06c-9fefdac989cb.mp3','NATIVE',11,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T07:58:23.886Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('5338a06e-bd70-409a-8c6d-140c0795aae0','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Fixed, Yaron. The missing pictures came from a real data-layer bug: four chains — Dirk, DekaMarkt, SPAR, and Jumbo — were fetching the product image from their APIs but the scrapers threw it away, so every variant for those chains had no image. I mapped the image they were already fetching for Dirk and DekaMarkt, re-scraped both, and the deals digest went from about two hundred missing images down to thirty-five — and those last thirty-five are AH voordeelshop non-grocery items like frying pans that genuinely have no photo. I verified the image URLs actually load and checked the live page in the browser; the top deals all have real product photos now. It''s committed. One honest heads-up: SPAR and Jumbo still have no images either — same bug, different scrapers — but they have basically no active deals so the digest is fully covered; their images only matter for search and comparison, which I left as a follow-up.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/5338a06e-bd70-409a-8c6d-140c0795aae0.mp3','NL-SUPER · IMAGES FIXED',49,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T07:58:30.649Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('bc4f97f7-5885-4627-b269-95732e85bdaf','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','I checked the code. No — pai-gmail doesn''t take any context each session. It''s a plain stateless command-line tool. Every time you run it, it just parses the flags, loads the OAuth token for the account you named from the config folder, hits the Gmail API, and prints the result. It doesn''t load the PAI brain, doesn''t read CLAUDE.md or the system prompt, and doesn''t carry any conversational state between runs. The only thing that persists on disk is your auth tokens — that''s the entire memory it has. So when I call it from inside a Claude session, it costs nothing against my context window beyond the text I choose to read back.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/bc4f97f7-5885-4627-b269-95732e85bdaf.mp3','NATIVE',34,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T07:58:51.556Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('608cc6ea-a8d5-4773-b7c8-7de1e467f588','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Building it now. Writing the pai-meet tool — the local whisper engine, the notes generator, the record and stop commands, and the storage — all matching your other pai CLIs. Then I''ll run the engine end to end on a real clip to prove it works before I hand it to you.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/608cc6ea-a8d5-4773-b7c8-7de1e467f588.mp3','REX — building pai-meet',14,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T08:00:04.092Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('84aa0e70-35df-4e0c-b327-62006fb99437','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Good catch to double-check, but the data backs it up — and to be precise, I said SPAR and Jumbo have no active deals, not Dirk. Dirk definitely has deals: 464 active right now, 409 of them food, which is exactly why fixing Dirk''s images mattered for the digest. The chains with zero active deals are SPAR, Jumbo, and Vomar — their APIs just don''t expose promotions. So only five of the eight chains run deals at all, and Albert Heijn plus Hoogvliet are the vast majority. Everything checks out.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/84aa0e70-35df-4e0c-b327-62006fb99437.mp3','NL-SUPER · DEALS PER CHAIN',27,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T08:01:06.964Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('79f7a86b-116d-409a-8e9f-d5717f472014','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Done — pai-meet is built and the engine is proven end to end. I tested the whole pipeline through the actual command: transcribe a clip, generate notes, browse it. English came out clean and faithful — it caught ship on Friday and the Q3 budget with nothing invented. Hebrew worked too: it auto-detected Hebrew and wrote the notes in Hebrew. The commands are all live — record, stop, transcribe, notes, list, show, setup, devices — sitting right next to your other pai tools. The one thing I couldn''t test myself is the live recording of a real call, because that needs BlackHole installed plus a reboot and microphone permission — that''s the two-minute setup step on your side, and pai-meet setup walks you through it. I also cleaned up the synthetic test meetings so your Meetings folder is empty and ready. And I''ve got Forge auditing the recording code in the background to catch anything I couldn''t test live. So: engine done and verified, your move is the BlackHole setup, then we record a real meeting.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/79f7a86b-116d-409a-8e9f-d5717f472014.mp3','REX — pai-meet built + verified',52,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T08:04:05.994Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('706aa00c-062d-41d1-8d71-2c1208bb80c3','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Forge earned its keep — it found six real high-severity bugs in the recording path, every one of which would''ve bitten on your first live call: an orphaned recorder if the config folder didn''t exist yet, trusting a stale transcript, two same-titled meetings overwriting each other, and a crash on very long meetings. I fixed all twelve findings and re-verified the engine still works end to end in both languages, with clean temp files and collision-proof naming. So the tool is now genuinely solid, not just working-on-my-machine. The recording path itself I still can''t run until BlackHole is installed — that''s your two-minute step — but the bugs that lived in it are gone. Net: pai-meet is built, audited, and hardened. Your move is brew install blackhole-2ch and a reboot, then we record a real meeting together.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/706aa00c-062d-41d1-8d71-2c1208bb80c3.mp3','REX — pai-meet hardened',42,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T08:15:19.167Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('25edb28e-bccd-4e23-98cb-58bcad1fbda7','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','The editable family roster is built and live. Tamar can now fill in her own family inside her own area — members moved from hardcoded source into the database, scoped per household, fully editable. I verified the security matrix end to end: Tamar is hard-walled to her own household, can''t read or write yours, foreign ids return not-found so they can''t be probed. The add and edit both work through the real UI — I caught and fixed a double-submit bug where a fast double-tap created two members, since kids can share a name there''s no natural dedupe so I guarded the handler. Your four boys seeded into the database, Tamar''s side starts empty with an Add-your-family prompt. Onboarding I parked as you said — it''s the future first-run flow that wraps this same create path, so nothing''s throwaway. Forge is running a security audit on the member API right now; I''ll fold in anything it finds and then commit. I''ll let you know the moment it''s back.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/25edb28e-bccd-4e23-98cb-58bcad1fbda7.mp3','FAMILY_OS · ROSTER BUILT',58,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T08:16:04.539Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('4c201de5-0ead-47f6-9374-9415e0031397','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Done — the whole thing is shipped, audited, and committed. To recap the session: I fixed the year-resolution date bug, corrected the boys'' names to Iftach and Yoval and added their ages and classes, and then built the editable family roster you asked for. Tamar can now fill in her own family inside her own area — members live in the database, scoped per household, fully editable. Forge ran a security audit on the new member API and it earned its keep again: isolation, CSRF, and injection were all clean, but it caught a real cross-household existence oracle that my own happy-path tests sailed right past — a quirk where supplying an existing id from the other household leaked that it existed. I fixed that and a validation gap, re-verified both, and committed everything. The app''s live, the roster''s editable, your four boys are in, Tamar''s side is ready and empty for her. Onboarding''s parked as the future first-run flow, and the next real thread is the Google Calendar sync — the step that pushes events out to your actual phones. That one needs your OAuth, so it''s yours to greenlight when you want it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/4c201de5-0ead-47f6-9374-9415e0031397.mp3','FAMILY_OS · ROSTER SHIPPED',64,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T08:24:58.770Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f1fce1b7-f303-4e2d-ac6b-b8ed689ec7a8','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Cracked it, Yaron. You were right — Jumbo absolutely has deals, we just weren''t getting them. Two bugs: the scraper only captured simple price-drops from the product search, which missed all the multi-buy bundles, and those few it did get had no end date so the view filtered them out. The real source is a separate folder query Jumbo exposes — three hundred and twenty-six promotions with proper start and end dates, the discount mechanism, and a product list whose IDs match ours exactly. I wired it in with an honesty gate so only real price deals count — brand groupings like Van Wijngaarden and delivery discounts get excluded. One nuance: Jumbo doesn''t publish absolute prices, we derive them and they''re often inflated, so for Jumbo bundles I show the trustworthy effective price instead of the bogus single. Result: Jumbo went from zero to one thousand five hundred seventy-three live deals on the page, dated and decoded. Two follow-ups: I need to push the scraper change to the always-on box, and SPAR and Vomar genuinely expose no deals through their APIs so we leave those, as you said.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f1fce1b7-f303-4e2d-ac6b-b8ed689ec7a8.mp3','NL-SUPER · JUMBO DEALS LIVE',56,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T08:29:10.168Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('0bf1b120-739c-4b97-8dd5-a97da861fef9','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Done — deployed to the box and verified. I pushed all three scraper changes, not just Jumbo: the Dirk and DekaMarkt image fixes had to go too, otherwise the box''s next scheduled scrape would''ve re-run the old code and wiped the product images I just backfilled. On the box, all three compile clean, and I confirmed the Jumbo folder query is reachable from the box''s datacenter IP — three hundred twenty-six promotions, HTTP two hundred — which was the one thing I wasn''t sure about since Jumbo throttles datacenter IPs. No package install needed. The production data is already current from today''s runs; the box now just maintains it. The next scheduled scrape is Wednesday at four in the morning and it''ll use the new code automatically. Nothing pending on this.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/0bf1b120-739c-4b97-8dd5-a97da861fef9.mp3','NL-SUPER · BOX DEPLOY DONE',39,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T08:37:27.259Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('591e46eb-d661-4209-8996-c197e4e74d92','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','You''re right, and I owe you that — I explained those buttons only in text and never spoke it. No excuse; every response is supposed to speak and I missed firing it. Here''s the answer out loud. Those four pills on the capture page — Photo of a Dutch school letter, Forwarded English email, Typed Hebrew note, and a birthday-party note — are not a real feature. They''re canned sample inputs, leftovers from when this was a self-contained demo. Tapping one drops a pre-written example into the note box and immediately runs the reader on it, so you could try the capture-to-extract magic in Dutch, English, or Hebrew without typing or photographing your own. One catch: the Photo of a Dutch school letter label is misleading — it doesn''t open the camera, it just pastes that letter''s text and reads it; the camera emoji is cosmetic. Since you and Tamar are using this for real now — same reason you dropped the demo events earlier — those buttons are really just clutter on the real capture screen. My recommendation is to remove them. Want me to pull them out?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/591e46eb-d661-4209-8996-c197e4e74d92.mp3','FAMILY_OS · VOICE FIX + ANSWER',63,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T08:37:51.723Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('e570b0c8-3e46-4045-93c4-87021caa9725','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','All saved, Yaron — you''re clear to start a new session. The repo''s clean with three commits in, everything''s live and verified, and the box is deployed. The resume pointer is updated as the top block, so a fresh session picks up exactly where we are: deals digest live, Jumbo deals flowing, and the open threads are the multi-buy radar, the deal hero, wiring the feed to auto-refresh on the box, the SPAR and Jumbo image capture, and the one that''s yours to decide — picking a brand name and domain to start the SEO clock. Good session. Talk soon.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/e570b0c8-3e46-4045-93c4-87021caa9725.mp3','SESSION CLOSE',28,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T08:39:27.208Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('c9268b68-9674-4073-9751-b06f7035c15a','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Removing the four sample buttons, and auditing the whole app for any other demo or simulated leftovers so we pull them all in one pass. I''ll show you what I find before deciding on anything that''s a real feature stub versus pure demo filler.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/c9268b68-9674-4073-9751-b06f7035c15a.mp3','FAMILY_OS · DEMO CLEANUP',16,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T08:41:01.936Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('fd478e56-49aa-4dda-9278-d2fc5f305724','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Entering the Algorithm. Good task — this is the growth and distribution side of NL Supermarkets, and it''s exactly the right time to build it. You gave me one seed, studentenkorting dot N L, a student-discount aggregator. I''m going to expand that into a real, verified map of Dutch organizations and websites where it makes sense to promote the grocery-deals platform. My plan: I''ll fan out a handful of parallel research agents, each covering a different family of channels — deals and coupon aggregators like your example, money-saving and frugal-living communities, organizations that serve budget-sensitive households like the budget institute and food banks, and high-affinity niche audiences like students, expats, and large families. Every entry comes back with a real verified link, who their audience is, why they fit, and how to approach them — including the discount-code partnership angle you mentioned. I''ll hold everything to verified-only, no invented names. Then I''ll rank them and write it into the project as a document you can act on.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/fd478e56-49aa-4dda-9278-d2fc5f305724.mp3','ALGORITHM ENTRY',55,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T08:44:38.620Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('386e3471-ac07-451d-a736-d5fcff93bfb4','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Hey Yaron, Nova here. I''ve pulled the full state on NL Supermarkets. Quick picture: the data layer is locked and healthy — eight chains, around ninety thousand variants, the cross-chain spine audited and self-updating on the Hetzner box. The consumer app, Scherp, is live at nl-supermarkets-app dot pages dot dev with three working surfaces: a full-catalog home search, the cross-chain compare, and as of today the deals digest at slash offers, all Forge-audited. So we''re genuinely close to a real launch. There are really only a few live threads worth your call. The big one is the launch gate — picking a real brand name and domain, because that starts the SEO clock and nothing else can substitute for it. Then there''s a data-layer bug: the dekamarkt scraper crashed on the four a.m. box run, though it ran clean for me later, so it may be transient. There''s also remaining polish — affiliate deep-links, SEO infrastructure, a trust layer — and two chains, SPAR and Jumbo, still showing placeholder images in search. Tell me where you want to push and I''ll dig in.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/386e3471-ac07-451d-a736-d5fcff93bfb4.mp3','NL-SUPERMARKETS',53,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T08:46:01.289Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('a7bd0092-d454-4eea-83b6-0290586c420f','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','The four sample buttons are gone and committed, and I deleted the old simulated extractor that was dead code behind them. The capture page is clean and verified. The audit turned up three more things, but they''re a different category — not samples, they''re simulated feature stubs. There''s a Settings banner that literally says the whole app is a simulation and everything''s faked, which is just wrong now since capture, storage, login and the roster are all real. There''s a panel on the event page showing a fake Google Calendar sync that says nothing leaves the app. And the entire Alerts screen is a reminder simulation with a fake test-reminder button. These are all placeholders for the real calendar sync and reminders coming in Slice four. Removing the Alerts page means dropping a whole nav screen, so that''s a structural call I want from you rather than just bulldozing it. I''ve put the options on screen — remove them all, keep them as honest coming-soon stubs, or just fix the wrong banner.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/a7bd0092-d454-4eea-83b6-0290586c420f.mp3','FAMILY_OS · SIM SURFACES',57,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T08:47:17.136Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('d18c0c80-8eab-4402-975d-b7337e28d37f','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Sure — tell me what you''d like to clarify. Whether you see these three as just more of the same demo stuff to remove, or you''ve got a different read on the Alerts screen and where reminders should live, or something about my framing that''s off. I''m listening.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/d18c0c80-8eab-4402-975d-b7337e28d37f.mp3','FAMILY_OS · CLARIFY',15,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T08:50:22.704Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('219093aa-3da4-4eaf-8b51-60826a8fa301','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Understood — we leave those three simulated surfaces for now and fix them when we build the real alerts, calendar sync, and settings. Now the real task: making the cards editable. After you pick a model, each card it produced should open to show everything and let you edit it — assign a kid with a picker, set an end time yourself, and adjust the rest. Let me read how those cards work right now so I build it onto what''s there instead of fighting it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/219093aa-3da4-4eaf-8b51-60826a8fa301.mp3','FAMILY_OS · EDITABLE CARDS',25,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T08:55:01.535Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('126988d2-387e-4944-8cd2-a562eecb07aa','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','All four research agents came back, and the result is much bigger than the one seed you gave me — about fifty verified Dutch channels across nine families, every one with a real working link, who they reach, and how to approach them. I wrote it all into the project as a document. The most useful thing I found is a reframe of your discount-code idea. A discount code is what you offer for a paid product, but ours is free, so a percentage-off doesn''t map. The thing that actually works for a free tool is a co-branded savings page for a partner''s members — for example, a cheapest-groceries-for-students page with Knaek, or a weekly-deals digest for the senior union ANBO. The real discount-and-affiliate model only kicks in later, once we build affiliate links into the supermarket chains themselves. Two more sharp findings. First, your easiest channels are partly your competitors — the folder sites and cashback apps already do pieces of what we do, so treat them as data partners, not billboards. Our wedge is the one thing none of them have: comparing the same product across all eight chains. Second, your very best channels won''t take money — the budget institute Nibud and the nutrition centre literally already tell people to compare supermarket prices using apps, so we are exactly what their advice points to; they give trust and search-ranking backlinks but they''re slow and strictly non-commercial. The one catch on all of this: don''t start outreach yet. The live site is still a no-index placeholder with no real brand or domain, and nobody links to a placeholder. So the list is loaded and ready to fire the moment you lock the real brand and domain — that''s the gate. I put a start-here shortlist of ten at the top, ranked by fit and ease, so the first moves are obvious.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/126988d2-387e-4944-8cd2-a562eecb07aa.mp3','ALGORITHM | SYNTHESIS',90,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T08:55:38.314Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('a15a9c65-915a-4013-9a85-a3b8267531cf','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Done. The channel map is written into the project, advisor-reviewed, and every link verified live. The two moves I''d lead with are the data-P-R index — a monthly cheapest-supermarket story the press will reprint — and the influencer shortlist starting with One Broke Girl. But nothing fires until you lock the real brand and domain. Want me to draft the actual outreach messages next, or design that cheapest-supermarket index?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/a15a9c65-915a-4013-9a85-a3b8267531cf.mp3','ALGORITHM | DONE',22,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T09:01:00.435Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('913bad54-800c-4871-b7bf-96d101d31a43','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Both done. The four sample buttons are gone along with the dead simulated extractor behind them, and I left the three simulated feature surfaces alone as you said — they get fixed when we build the real alerts, calendar sync, and settings. Then the main thing: the cards after you pick a model are now fully editable. Each one opens with everything visible and editable — the title, date, start and end time, location, the to-do, and notes. The who field is now a row of kid chips you tap to assign one or more children, and the kid the model named is already pre-selected in their colour. And there''s a dedicated Ends field so you can add a finish time yourself even when the invitation only gives a start. I verified it live: I typed a note for Uri, picked Gemma, his chip was pre-selected, I added Iftach with a tap and set an end time of three p.m., confirmed, and the saved event came back with both boys and the end time exactly right. It''s committed and live. Next real step is still the Google Calendar sync whenever you want to greenlight the OAuth.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/913bad54-800c-4871-b7bf-96d101d31a43.mp3','FAMILY_OS · EDITABLE CARDS DONE',62,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T09:02:12.788Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('68044833-0748-4ad6-bc9d-14d1fc093ead','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Entering the Algorithm. I''m taking on the dekamarkt scraper crash. My read going in: the four a.m. box run died with a GraphQL gateway rejection and zero items, but the same scraper pulled all nine and a half thousand items clean for me later — so this smells transient, not a permanent break. The real bug is probably that the scraper crashes hard on a transient rejection instead of retrying, exactly the class of failure the Jumbo scraper had. I''m reproducing it live now and reading the fetch code in parallel before I commit to a fix.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/68044833-0748-4ad6-bc9d-14d1fc093ead.mp3','OBSERVE',28,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T09:34:00.891Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('e4b87d36-3306-43f5-a518-3180de821704','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Saved. I wrote a focused memory capturing the promotion-channel map and the four strategic findings — the discount-code reframe, easiest-channels-are-competitors, best-channels-won''t-take-money, and data-P-R as the highest-leverage move — plus the hard gate that nothing fires until the real brand and domain are live. I also updated the resume pointer so a fresh session picks this thread up cleanly. You''re clear to start a new session whenever — just clear and go.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/e4b87d36-3306-43f5-a518-3180de821704.mp3','SESSION CLOSE',23,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T09:34:19.007Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('3fa6ac0d-9c5a-4047-9012-c5351539a98b','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Confirmed it cold. The box journal shows dekamarkt died in one second with zero items on the morning run, while five days earlier it pulled ninety-five hundred items clean. So the gateway is fine — it was a transient fast-rejection, almost certainly a four-oh-three throttle on the datacenter IP, hitting the very first call. And the bug is exactly what I suspected: dekamarkt''s retry filter is the old narrow one that doesn''t recognize a four-oh-three or a GraphQL-level rejection as retryable, so it crashed where Jumbo would have backed off and retried. Jumbo already got this exact fix five days ago. I''m mirroring that proven matcher into dekamarkt now, then typechecking, running it locally to prove the happy path, having Forge review it, and deploying to the box.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/3fa6ac0d-9c5a-4047-9012-c5351539a98b.mp3','EXECUTE',40,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T09:37:42.009Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('c3c35f2c-9949-43d0-a145-182a0af7c180','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Everything''s confirmed and ready for the one step only you can do. BlackHole is a system audio driver, so it needs your Mac password — I can''t type that for you. In the prompt, run: bang, brew install blackhole-2ch, and-and sudo killall coreaudiod. The first installs the virtual cable; the second reloads macOS audio so BlackHole shows up immediately, no reboot needed — that''s the trick that skips the restart. It''ll ask for your Mac login password. If the password prompt acts up through the bang, just run the same line in a normal Terminal. Then say done, and I take over: I''ll verify BlackHole appeared, script the Multi-Output device for you so you don''t have to click through Audio MIDI Setup, point pai-meet at the right devices, and run a live recording test to prove the record and stop path actually works. After that you''re ready for a real meeting.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/c3c35f2c-9949-43d0-a145-182a0af7c180.mp3','REX — install BlackHole, your step',43,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T09:38:26.525Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('ee2e8bdf-6cda-4df5-be64-a992ef3d1cf9','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Got it. You want the full FBTO picture — total health insurance spend over the last two years. I''m going to pull the payments from your bank, then cross-check against the actual invoices on the FBTO site, and fall back to your yaronkra5 inbox if the invoices aren''t on their portal. Starting now.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/ee2e8bdf-6cda-4df5-be64-a992ef3d1cf9.mp3','ALGORITHM | FBTO Spend Investigation',15,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T09:38:43.715Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('2b6719ac-ba26-42c8-9cf4-dd1136f13ee1','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Entering the Observe phase.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/2b6719ac-ba26-42c8-9cf4-dd1136f13ee1.mp3','OBSERVE',2,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T09:39:24.916Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7cdafbce-aaf7-4d7c-8dfa-0ad661977129','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Both sessions are live — your bank is Revolut and the FBTO health portal is open. I can''t drive the tabs you opened by hand, so I''m opening my own controlled tab to the same FBTO portal; the login carries over since it''s the same Chrome. My plan: pull the premium and invoice history from FBTO first since that''s the authoritative billed amount, then search your Revolut transactions for the actual FBTO debits to confirm what really left your account, and if the portal is thin on invoices I''ll check your yaronkra5 inbox. Starting with the FBTO portal now.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7cdafbce-aaf7-4d7c-8dfa-0ad661977129.mp3','THINK + PLAN',31,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T09:41:02.051Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('c911df0f-60bd-4863-b818-1574c7df0bb8','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','The fix is in and looking strong. The local run came back clean — ninety-five seventy-one items, exit zero, nothing wrongly delisted. Forge reviewed it and confirmed the retry fix is at exact parity with the proven Jumbo version, then caught something better: dekamarkt was missing the delist safeguard that Jumbo has, which meant a few throttled subgroups could silently wipe live products. I added that guard too — count failed subgroups, skip delisting if the walk was partial. The fix is deployed to the box and I''m running it there now from the datacenter IP, the exact environment where it crashed, plus an advisor check. I''ll confirm the moment both come back.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/c911df0f-60bd-4863-b818-1574c7df0bb8.mp3','VERIFY',34,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T09:44:09.087Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('fad76879-cfdb-4205-9e07-a43a1bf65ee3','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Almost there — good news, BlackHole installed perfectly, the driver''s on disk. The only thing that didn''t happen is the audio daemon restart; the earlier command chain dropped the sudo half, so coreaudiod is still running the old config from two weeks ago. I tried to restart it myself but your sudo isn''t cached, so I can''t. One command fixes it: bang, sudo killall coreaudiod. Enter your Mac password, and BlackHole shows up instantly since it''s already installed. Then say done and I''ll verify it, build the Multi-Output device, configure pai-meet, and run the live recording test. If it somehow still doesn''t appear, a reboot is the sure fallback.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/fad76879-cfdb-4205-9e07-a43a1bf65ee3.mp3','REX — restart coreaudiod',34,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T09:44:19.584Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('c4115695-242d-4de8-8ea6-8bf9c678de18','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Here''s what the FBTO portal tells me so far. Your current premium is three hundred one euros a month — two ninety seven fifty plus a three fifty module. But the portal''s financial overview only keeps a rolling window of the last five months, and your message box goes back to mid-August 2025 with claims, so you were already insured with FBTO in 2025. The portal won''t hand me two clean years on its own. So I''m going to your Revolut now to find the actual FBTO debits — that tells me exactly when payments started and the real total that left your account.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/c4115695-242d-4de8-8ea6-8bf9c678de18.mp3','EXECUTE | Pivot to bank',32,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T09:44:22.425Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('234f1e43-c447-4cd1-988e-bfe0b3f80242','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','One snag on the bank — Revolut locks the web app behind your passcode, and the tab I opened is asking for it. I won''t type that for you. When you get a sec, type your passcode into the new Revolut tab I just opened, and tell me to continue. I''m not waiting around though — I''m going into your yaronkra5 inbox right now to pull every FBTO invoice and payment confirmation, which gives me the payment history independent of the bank.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/234f1e43-c447-4cd1-988e-bfe0b3f80242.mp3','EXECUTE | Bank needs passcode',22,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T09:45:23.489Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('beb346a8-eff4-48ea-a2ba-0100d1143059','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Okay, Google Calendar sync. Here''s the shape of it. It''s one-way — the app stays the source of truth and pushes your confirmed events out to Google, where they show up on your phone. It''s per household: you connect your own Google account from Settings, Tamar connects hers, and each household''s events only ever go to that owner''s calendar — never crossed. When you confirm an event it gets created in Google, when you edit it updates, when you delete it disappears, all tracked by storing the Google event id on our row. Google''s own popup and email reminders ride along for free, so basic reminders come with it; the richer Telegram reminders I''d do as a separate follow-up. The one thing only you can do is create the Google Cloud OAuth client — I can''t make that, it needs your console. I''ve opened a credentials file for you to paste the client id and secret into once you''ve made it, and I''ll walk you through the steps on screen. I recommend we ship calendar sync first and do real reminders after. Once the credentials are in, I''ll build the whole thing — token storage encrypted in the database, the connect flow, and the push-on-save — and then we''ll watch a real test event land on your actual calendar. Take a look and tell me if the shape''s right.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/beb346a8-eff4-48ea-a2ba-0100d1143059.mp3','FAMILY_OS · SLICE 4 PLAN',72,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T09:45:26.251Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('ef6af2f4-843b-408b-aa88-4c1d7db92b02','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Done, and it''s solid. The dekamarkt crash is fixed and verified end to end. Root cause was exactly the transient-rejection class Jumbo already had — dekamarkt''s retry filter didn''t recognize a four-oh-three or a GraphQL throttle as retryable, so it crashed where Jumbo would back off. I widened the matcher to Jumbo parity, and while Forge was reviewing it caught something more dangerous than the crash: dekamarkt was missing the delist safeguard, so a few throttled subgroups could silently wipe live products from the catalog. I armed that guard too, and made it default-safe per the advisor. Verified with a real box run from the datacenter IP — ninety-five seventy-one items, clean exit, nothing wrongly delisted — typecheck clean, committed locally, and re-synced to the box so Wednesday''s four a.m. run uses it. One honest caveat: the box run passed without actually hitting a four-oh-three this time, so the recovery path is proven by Jumbo parity and the unit test rather than a forced live block. And the bigger pattern worth a follow-up: this same bug class is now confirmed in two of eight scrapers, so the other six are worth auditing — Dirk first, since it shares Deka''s gateway.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/ef6af2f4-843b-408b-aa88-4c1d7db92b02.mp3','LEARN',60,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T09:50:21.810Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('db98b597-b188-4b16-9b27-8acea73d06b7','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','It works. The live test captured the system audio perfectly through BlackHole — it transcribed the test sentence about the quarterly numbers and shipping Friday, correctly labeled as the other side, while your mic came through as your own channel. So the record-and-stop path is now proven live: both sides captured, both correctly labeled. The only artifact is that on a silent mic track Whisper sometimes invents a short phrase like thank you — harmless, and in a real meeting your actual words fill that channel. Now I''m wiring the last bit of automation: record will automatically flip your audio output to the capture device, and stop will flip it back, so you never open Sound settings — one command to record a meeting. Give me a moment to wire and re-test it hands-free.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/db98b597-b188-4b16-9b27-8acea73d06b7.mp3','REX — live capture works',39,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T09:57:09.805Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('d0a5eb72-a4f1-44a3-8135-2bd41bd7ce97','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Cracked the bank. Your FBTO premium is debited straight from your Revolut euro account on the first of each month — three hundred one euros, and the reference even spells out your FBTO relation number and the coverage period. Revolut''s web app fights automation hard, but I found that its statement generator hands back a signed download link I can pull directly. I''m now regenerating the full statement from August 2024 to now so I can list every single FBTO debit and total them.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/d0a5eb72-a4f1-44a3-8135-2bd41bd7ce97.mp3','EXECUTE | Bank cracked',28,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T09:57:54.599Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('a8dcec52-7fe7-4b8e-a360-8aeedda3cc84','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Opening it now — that''s the google-oauth dot env file in TextEdit. Paste the client id and client secret onto the two empty lines at the bottom, save it, and tell me when it''s filled. The redirect URI and scope you need for the Google console are right there in the comments at the top.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/a8dcec52-7fe7-4b8e-a360-8aeedda3cc84.mp3','FAMILY_OS · OAUTH FILE',18,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T10:02:14.976Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('455ca19b-056e-4ac5-ac26-4a433c0190e4','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Done — and the number is solid because it''s cross-checked three ways. Here''s the bottom line. Since you switched to FBTO on the 19th of September 2024, you''ve paid them six thousand seven hundred thirty euros in total — that''s six thousand two hundred fifty-two in monthly premiums across twenty-two months, plus four hundred seventy-eight in deductible care costs. FBTO paid you back four hundred forty in care-cost reimbursements, so your true net spend on FBTO is six thousand two hundred ninety euros. The premium climbed each year: two sixty-seven a month in 2024, two ninety-five in 2025, and three-oh-one now in 2026, and it covers both you and Noa, with the four kids free. Two honest caveats. First, there''s no FBTO spend before September 2024 — you simply weren''t with them yet, so ''the last two years'' is really the full FBTO history of about twenty-one months. Second, the FBTO website only keeps a rolling few months of invoices, so the bank statement was the real backbone here — but where they overlap, the portal and the bank match to the cent. I''ve written you a full month-by-month breakdown you can analyze next.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/455ca19b-056e-4ac5-ac26-4a433c0190e4.mp3','COMPLETE | FBTO Spend',62,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T10:05:12.033Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('15c0b951-2cad-4862-83e1-2b3f9bb14cda','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','You''re fully ready. BlackHole''s installed and loaded, I scripted the Multi-Output device through CoreAudio so you never touched Audio MIDI Setup, and the whole thing now runs hands-free. I proved it end to end: you type pai-meet record, it automatically flips your audio to the capture device, records both sides, and when you type pai-meet stop it flips your headphones back, transcribes locally, and writes notes — it even pulled out the action item on its own. One real issue I hit and fixed: your Bluetooth headset shows up as two devices with the same name, which was breaking the audio switching, so I rewrote it to match devices by their unique ID instead — now it''s rock solid. I also made the setup command rebuild the audio device automatically in case it doesn''t survive a reboot. Your audio''s back to normal, the test recordings are cleaned up. The only thing left is the real proof: record an actual meeting. Just run pai-meet record before your next call.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/15c0b951-2cad-4862-83e1-2b3f9bb14cda.mp3','REX — pai-meet fully live',48,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T10:07:17.673Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('c665c81e-6288-4033-88e6-7d08d580377f','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Got the credentials. Building the calendar sync now — the database tables, the OAuth connect flow, encrypted token storage, and the push that mirrors every confirmed event to Google. I''ll set the secrets, deploy, verify the mechanical parts, and run a Forge security audit on the token handling before you connect your real account. Then you''ll click Connect once and we''ll watch a test event land on your calendar.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/c665c81e-6288-4033-88e6-7d08d580377f.mp3','FAMILY_OS · BUILDING SYNC',25,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T10:10:50.277Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('24603342-57e0-488f-8f44-a5f6108adf3d','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Here''s my honest read. The app is built and working — search, comparison, and the deals digest are all live and audited. But it''s sitting behind a noindex placeholder with no real brand and no real domain. That''s the ninety-percent line you keep landing on — fully built, never quite shipped. So my recommendation for the next step is unambiguous: launch it. Not more features, not the image fixes — those don''t block anything. The whole acquisition thesis is SEO, and SEO has a long fuse: Google takes weeks to crawl, index, and rank a brand-new domain. Every week it stays behind noindex is a week that clock isn''t running. The only thing actually blocking launch is your call — the brand name and the domain. Everything after that is mechanical: flip noindex, add the sitemap and canonical tags, wire the affiliate links so revenue is on from day one, and ship. So the concrete next move I''d make is to hand you a shortlist of brand names with the dot-N-L domains already checked for availability, so you''re picking from real options instead of a blank page. Want me to generate that? There''s also a second lever worth naming — the B2B shelf-monitor is the faster path to actual paying revenue, but it''s a fresh build off to the side. I''d finish the consumer launch first, since it''s nearly free to cross the line.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/24603342-57e0-488f-8f44-a5f6108adf3d.mp3','NEXT STEP',64,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T10:11:57.392Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('9cc116e2-b74f-43e9-a950-50edea0300a8','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Building you a single self-contained HTML report now — headline numbers up top, a chart showing your spend climbing to six thousand seven hundred thirty euros, the premium stepping up each year, and full tables for every premium, care cost, and refund. I''ll open it in Chrome to confirm it renders before handing it over.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/9cc116e2-b74f-43e9-a950-50edea0300a8.mp3','BUILD | FBTO HTML report',18,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T10:17:16.346Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('0901eb59-ca62-4abc-9239-04f43c7865f5','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Your report is ready and I''ve confirmed it renders cleanly in Chrome. It''s a single self-contained HTML file — open it and you get the four headline numbers up top, a chart showing your spend climbing to six thousand seven hundred thirty euros with the net line dipping where FBTO refunded you, a spend-by-year breakdown, the premium step-up from two sixty-seven to three-oh-one a month, and full tables for all twenty-two premiums plus every care cost and refund. It''s at fbto-spend-overview dot html in your Downloads. Ready when you want to dig into the analysis.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/0901eb59-ca62-4abc-9239-04f43c7865f5.mp3','COMPLETE | FBTO HTML report',31,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T10:19:29.192Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('fc87ae4f-b25c-4960-8c6a-a916728fae82','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Done — the recorder now saves MP3 instead of WAV, and it''s a big win: about five times smaller, so a one-hour meeting drops from a couple hundred megabytes to around forty for both tracks. I verified whisper transcribes the MP3 directly with no loss in accuracy, and the hands-free record-and-stop flow still works exactly the same. The bitrate is set to forty-eight k, tunable in config if you ever want smaller or higher quality. Everything''s cleaned up and ready. So that''s the efficiency change you asked for, in and proven.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/fc87ae4f-b25c-4960-8c6a-a916728fae82.mp3','REX — MP3 recording',29,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T10:21:39.191Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('02b93afb-4b87-43e6-bd64-036b43ab9ae7','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','The calendar sync is built, deployed, and the connect button is live in Settings. I verified everything I can without your consent: the worker builds the right Google authorization URL with the correct scope and callback, the status endpoint sees the credentials, and isolation holds — Tamar can''t touch your household''s connection, anonymous gets blocked. The one step left is yours: clicking Connect and allowing it on Google''s screen, which stores your account. But hold off for just a moment — Forge is auditing the OAuth and token-encryption code right now, the same security pass that caught real issues on the last two slices. I don''t want a real refresh token stored before that clears. As soon as Forge comes back and I''ve folded in anything it finds, I''ll give you the green light to connect, and then we''ll watch a test event land on your actual calendar.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/02b93afb-4b87-43e6-bd64-036b43ab9ae7.mp3','FAMILY_OS · SYNC READY · HOLD FOR AUDIT',50,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T10:23:09.510Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('96aff9c3-727f-422a-84b9-f5a6b91e3315','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Let''s do it. First, my naming philosophy for this one, because the name has to carry the positioning. Your design research already ruled out the coupon-cheap trap — orange, yellow, words like goedkoop or discount. The brand should feel sharp and trustworthy and smart, not cheap. So I''m generating across a few distinct directions: the sharp-price angle, which is scherp, your working name; the honest-price angle, eerlijke prijs, which directly names your real moat — honest per-unit pricing; the smart-basket angle; the price-guide-or-radar angle; and a few short coined names that are easier to own and trademark. The hard constraint is reality: the dot-N-L space is mature, so most single dictionary words are already taken. That''s why I''m checking availability live before I show you anything — there''s no point falling in love with a name you can''t register. I''m verifying my domain-check method right now, then I''ll run the whole list and come back with only the real, registerable options, ranked, with my pick.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/96aff9c3-727f-422a-84b9-f5a6b91e3315.mp3','BRAND',50,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T10:24:39.263Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('14c299e0-2a8e-4271-bc59-40e34e87b28c','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Here''s where I landed. I checked twenty-three names live, and as expected every clean dictionary word is already gone — scherp, prijswijzer, prijsradar, they''re all registered. The good news is the compounds are open, and I''ve got six confirmed-available across every direction. My recommendation is PrijsScherp — prijsscherp dot N-L. Here''s the reasoning: because your whole growth plan is SEO, a name that carries the Dutch search word for price, prijs, is a genuine advantage — people literally search for prijzen and boodschappen. Scherp keeps the sharp, trustworthy feeling you already designed the brand around, and it preserves the equity of the Scherp working name you''ve been using. So it''s brand and SEO in one word, and the domain is free. The strong alternatives are SlimBoodschappen if you want warmer and friendlier, KassaScherp if you want something more distinctive and ownable, and PrijsChecker if you want the name to just flatly say what the site does. Before you actually register whichever one you pick, I''ll check the matching dot-com for brand protection and do a quick trademark and Google sanity check so we don''t walk into an existing brand. Tell me which direction speaks to you and I''ll lock it in.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/14c299e0-2a8e-4271-bc59-40e34e87b28c.mp3','BRAND PICK',60,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T10:28:07.615Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('3aed8a93-580a-4a76-a801-5bcc12dc69ab','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Love it. Here''s how I''ll run this. The part that has to be exact — parsing all thirty-four hundred transactions and totaling them — I''ll do myself with real code and check that the running balance reconciles, so the numbers are trustworthy. The slow, independent part — generating the Flux images — I''m kicking off right now as a background agent so it works in parallel while I analyze. Then I aggregate everything into one rich HTML report with charts, a money-flow breakdown, category analysis, your recurring subscriptions, trends over the twenty-two months, and the generated imagery woven in. Starting by reading the exact statement format so the parser is bulletproof.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/3aed8a93-580a-4a76-a801-5bcc12dc69ab.mp3','ALGORITHM E4 | Full transaction analysis',35,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T10:29:28.814Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('bbdc7683-0440-44d6-b456-befa30428b14','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Green light. Forge found three medium security issues and they were exactly worth holding for — two of them broke household isolation. One, a relayed connect link that could attach your Google account to the wrong household; two, a crafted event-id collision that could leak another household''s event into an attacker''s calendar; three, a weak-key fallback in the token encryption. I fixed all three — the OAuth flow is now bound to the browser that started it with a one-time cookie, the sync read is locked to the owning household, and the encryption refuses to run without a strong key and binds each token to its household. I also caught a nasty one of my own: a trailing newline had snuck into the stored client id, which Google would have rejected the instant you connected. Re-set clean. Everything''s verified and committed. So now it''s yours: open Settings, click Connect Google Calendar, and allow it on Google''s screen. You''ll see an unverified-app warning — that''s expected, click through it. Once you''re back and it says connected, confirm any event with a date and we''ll watch it appear on your real calendar.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/bbdc7683-0440-44d6-b456-befa30428b14.mp3','FAMILY_OS · GREEN LIGHT · CONNECT',64,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T10:34:23.166Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('c2e0bbb4-e557-4e7b-88b7-517b87c43151','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Big picture is in, and it''s a genuinely interesting story. Over these twenty-three months, two hundred ninety-six thousand euros flowed into this account and two hundred fifty-six thousand flowed out, and the balance grew from zero to about forty thousand. But here''s the real finding: only ninety-three thousand of that outflow was actual day-to-day spending — about four thousand fifty euros a month. Everything else was capital moving around — currency exchange, savings, investments, and two big unidentified payees, MMX and someone called A Ravindran, that together account for sixty thousand euros you''ll want to label. Your biggest real living cost is the international school, then groceries, then insurance. The four Flux images came out beautifully. I''m assembling the full report now with all the charts.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/c2e0bbb4-e557-4e7b-88b7-517b87c43151.mp3','EXECUTE | Analysis complete, building report',41,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T10:44:55.537Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('562fe06e-d104-49d5-9a85-bc73ccf74dcf','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','On it. Checking dot-com brand protection and trademark for both PrijsScherp and EerlijkPrijs, plus what''s sitting on the taken eerlijke-prijs domain, since a clipped name living right next to an active brand would be a problem.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/562fe06e-d104-49d5-9a85-bc73ccf74dcf.mp3','BRAND CHECK',12,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T10:45:07.156Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('65bd4755-3676-41f8-851d-54a8382a5a32','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','It works. The sync is live. I created a test event called Family OS sync test, dated tomorrow at two p.m., and within a few seconds Google''s calendar accepted it and handed back its own event id, which we stored on our row. That''s the proof — the event is now on your real Google Calendar under your aitheroad account. Go look — it should be there tomorrow, June tenth, two to three p.m. This is the make-it-leave-the-app moment: you confirm something in Family OS and it shows up on your actual phone calendar. When you''ve seen it, say the word and I''ll delete the test event, which also exercises the delete-sync path and cleans it off your calendar. Slice four is real.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/65bd4755-3676-41f8-851d-54a8382a5a32.mp3','FAMILY_OS · SYNC LIVE',41,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T10:46:40.015Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('325a67f7-d68c-46ce-acdc-f57346a0fb64','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Your full analysis is ready — open index dot html in the revolut-analysis folder in Downloads. It opens with the hero image and six headline numbers, then the key finding: of the two hundred fifty-six thousand that left the account, only ninety-three thousand was real spending — about four thousand fifty a month — and the rest was capital moving around. Below that you get a donut of your real spending categories, where the international school is your single biggest living cost ahead of groceries and insurance, a month-by-month cash-flow chart, your balance trajectory showing the account runs near empty until a recent forty-thousand-euro buffer, where your income came from, your top and most-frequent merchants, your recurring subscriptions, the biggest single payments, and a red-flagged section listing the unidentified payees — MMX at thirty-three thousand and A Ravindran at twenty-seven thousand — for you to label. Everything reconciles to within four tenths of a percent of Revolut''s own stated totals, and all four images were generated locally with Flux. The whole thing is one self-contained folder you can keep.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/325a67f7-d68c-46ce-acdc-f57346a0fb64.mp3','COMPLETE | Revolut analysis report',59,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T10:48:52.234Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('37b22007-6892-4aad-8c50-fcfec77d4013','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Confirmed both directions. Your Hebrew event synced to your calendar, my test event synced and is now deleted so it''ll disappear from your view. Slice four is fully done and verified — Family OS now genuinely pushes your confirmed events to your real Google Calendar. One small thing I noticed: two events you''d confirmed before connecting — the traffic lessons and garden volunteering — aren''t on Google, because sync only fires forward from when you connect. I can add a one-time backfill to push your existing events up if you want them there. Otherwise, the open threads from here are real reminders over Telegram, cleaning up those three parked simulation surfaces now that the calendar is genuinely real, and Tamar connecting her own Google account the same way you just did. Your call on what''s next.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/37b22007-6892-4aad-8c50-fcfec77d4013.mp3','FAMILY_OS · SLICE 4 DONE',47,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T10:52:32.989Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('b01f144e-b25d-4a7e-9884-3fda2b3d0d1b','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Good plan. I''ll clean up the simulated surfaces first, then build real Telegram reminders. One sequencing note: the Alerts screen is the one that actually becomes the real reminders page, so I''ll rebuild it as part of the reminders work instead of cleaning it twice. Right now I''m fixing the Settings banner that wrongly says nothing connects to Google, and removing the fake where-this-goes panel on the event page. Then I''ll lay out the reminders design — there are a couple of choices that are yours, like exactly when reminders fire and whether to use your existing Ringo bot or a dedicated Family OS one.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/b01f144e-b25d-4a7e-9884-3fda2b3d0d1b.mp3','FAMILY_OS · CLEANUP + REMINDERS',38,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T10:55:56.443Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('118d0905-5759-45c7-958a-37f6c6065e47','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Let me dig into that one. Stichting Confessioneel Onderwijs is Dutch for a foundation for faith-based education, and yours says Leiden. I''m pulling the exact reference lines from your statement to see the IBAN and any school name, and checking the web to confirm what it is and what it runs.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/118d0905-5759-45c7-958a-37f6c6065e47.mp3','RESEARCH | Stichting Confessioneel Onderwijs',15,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T10:58:49.720Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('eacc72d1-afbb-4655-bd30-3216abea25ba','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Cleanup''s done and verified — the simulation banner and the fake sync panel are gone, and Settings now correctly shows you connected to Google. Now for real reminders. The plan: a scheduled job runs every fifteen minutes, looks at your dated events and deadlines, and sends a Telegram message for any reminder that''s come due, then marks it sent so it never repeats. Each household gets its own Telegram chat — yours to you, Tamar''s to her. The Alerts screen becomes the real view of upcoming and sent reminders. Two choices are yours before I build: first, the bot — I can reuse your existing Ringo bot right now since I already have your chat id, or you can spin up a dedicated Family OS bot in BotFather; second, the timing — when do you actually want to be nudged. I''ve put both on screen with my recommendations.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/eacc72d1-afbb-4655-bd30-3216abea25ba.mp3','FAMILY_OS · REMINDERS PLAN',49,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T10:59:38.350Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('9d2b427a-5816-401a-9b07-c143ad84932f','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','On it. I''m going into your Yaron Kra 5 Gmail to pull every Ziggo email I can find. Ziggo''s your internet provider, and you think the plan ends in about a month — so I''m reading everything to understand your contract, the price, and the end date before we talk options.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/9d2b427a-5816-401a-9b07-c143ad84932f.mp3','NATIVE — Ziggo mail dig',14,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:00:33.564Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('9e221583-d087-46d3-9621-921f28effd87','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','All saved. The pai-meet tool is on disk, your config and the audio device are set, and I''ve written a full memory note so next session picks up exactly where we are — it''s live and hands-free, recording MP3 in both Hebrew and English. Two things waiting for next time: actually recording a real meeting to prove it in the wild, and building door two, the self-hosted Attendee bot for the meetings you''re not in. Good session. Talk soon.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/9e221583-d087-46d3-9621-921f28effd87.mp3','REX — saved, see you next time',21,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T11:03:06.378Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('3e50813b-f9bd-443b-bd52-56b113d8797d','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Okay, I went through your Yaron Kra 5 inbox and pulled the full Ziggo history. Here''s the headline, and it matters: your plan does not end in a month. Back on the twenty-ninth of November last year you did an upgrade — your old Internet XXL plan stopped and you moved to a plan called Wifi Middel, four hundred megabit download, at forty-seven fifty a month. And that upgrade started a fresh twelve-month minimum term. So you''re actually locked in until the end of November twenty-twenty-six, not July. If you cancel before then, Ziggo charges an early-exit buyout fee for the remaining months. My read is you''re either remembering the old contract from before that upgrade, or you''re mixing it up with the house move this summer. And the move is really the clean decision point — under Dutch rules, if you move and Ziggo can''t deliver at the new Delft address, that''s your window to cancel without penalty. So before we pick a direction, two things I want from you: when and where exactly you''re moving, and whether you want me to log into My Ziggo to read the exact end date and current price straight from the source. Tell me that and I''ll map out stay, switch to fiber, or time it to the move. Details are on screen.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/3e50813b-f9bd-443b-bd52-56b113d8797d.mp3','NATIVE — Ziggo findings',58,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:04:02.411Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('4bc61504-e475-4efc-ba6c-625fe61d65ce','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','On it — diving into your yaronkra5 Gmail to hunt down the EasyActive emails. Let me find them and I''ll tell you what''s there so we can send the reply.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/4bc61504-e475-4efc-ba6c-625fe61d65ce.mp3','GMAIL · EasyActive',9,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T11:05:04.056Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('29be9048-5c41-45d9-ae7b-9597ab8269ca','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Okay, found them — and here''s the thing. The Easy Active emails are all about your gym, Fitnessclub Easy Active in Leiderdorp. Back on April eighth you asked to cancel, they sent you the cancellation form, you filled it in and signed it, and they confirmed the termination. Your membership officially ended on May twelfth — so it''s already a month gone. From their side, everything''s closed. There''s no open email waiting for a reply, and nothing newer than April. So before I send anything, tell me what you actually want to send them — because the cancellation itself is already done and dusted.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/29be9048-5c41-45d9-ae7b-9597ab8269ca.mp3','GMAIL · Easy Active — cancellation already done',29,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T11:06:32.392Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('4510ac9b-0a8a-44e8-95df-37e8f1bd52e4','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Right, let''s go to the source. I''m opening My Ziggo in your real Chrome session to read the exact contract end date — the precise day your internet would stop if you do nothing. If you''re already logged in this is instant; if it asks for a login, I''ll pause and let you sign in yourself rather than handle your password. One moment.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/4510ac9b-0a8a-44e8-95df-37e8f1bd52e4.mp3','NATIVE — Mijn Ziggo login',16,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:06:47.775Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('efd44da7-d81f-44b3-b3d3-a0e1537d7081','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','The portal kicked us to the login screen — you''re signed out. The login window is open in Chrome right now. I won''t touch your password. Two clean ways in: you can just type your password in that Chrome window yourself, and I''ll pick it up the moment you''re in. Or, since I can read your Yaron Kra 5 Gmail, I can use the passwordless login — Ziggo emails you a code, I grab it, and we''re in without any password at all. Your call. Which way do you want to do this?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/efd44da7-d81f-44b3-b3d3-a0e1537d7081.mp3','NATIVE — Ziggo login choice',21,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:07:51.033Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('1157b50e-ffc0-49a2-ae43-dbf923c635c8','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Here''s your answer. The last time Easy Active took money from your Revolut account was April ninth, fifty-seven ninety-five. And that payment covered the period from April fourteenth to May twelfth — which is exactly when your membership ended. Since that charge, two hundred and fifty transactions have gone through your account, and not a single one is Easy Active. So they stopped billing you correctly, the final payment lined up perfectly with the cancellation date, and there''s nothing to dispute. You''re clean. Honestly, unless you saw something specific that worried you, there''s nothing we actually need to send them.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/1157b50e-ffc0-49a2-ae43-dbf923c635c8.mp3','GMAIL · Easy Active — last charge Apr 9, billing clean',30,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T11:12:22.598Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('41c51bdc-b6bf-42a3-aa2d-258df31c0e76','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Both done. The three simulated surfaces are cleaned — the false Settings banner and the fake sync panel are gone, and the Alerts screen is rebuilt as the real reminders page. And real Telegram reminders are live: a scheduled job runs every fifteen minutes, and for any dated event or deadline it sends you a nudge the evening before and the morning of, through your Ringo bot, deduplicated so nothing repeats. I verified the whole pipeline end to end — you got a test reminder, and I created a today event, triggered the run, and a real reminder landed on your Telegram, then a second run correctly sent nothing. The Alerts page now shows your real upcoming reminders with their exact fire times. Forge is auditing the reminder code right now — the scheduler, the send path, and the new endpoints — and I''ll fold in anything it finds. After that, the remaining bits are small: Tamar connecting her own Telegram, and an optional backfill of your pre-connect events. I''ll ping you when Forge is back.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/41c51bdc-b6bf-42a3-aa2d-258df31c0e76.mp3','FAMILY_OS · REMINDERS LIVE',60,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T11:12:43.229Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('d05f8b42-7ce5-4ffe-b587-68d1b0aabe24','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Got it from the source. Your contract end date is the twenty-eighth of November, twenty twenty-six. That''s official — it''s printed on your Ziggo contract page. So your internet does not stop in a month; you''re committed for about five and a half more months. And to be clear, nothing switches off on that date by itself — after the twenty-eighth of November the contract just rolls to month-to-month, and you can cancel any time with one month''s notice. Cancel before that date and you pay an early-exit fee, roughly the remaining months. Here''s what actually matters for you: your move to Delft this summer lands right in the middle of the contract. When you move you notify Ziggo, and because Delft has cable they''ll most likely just transfer the same contract to the new address and the clock keeps running to November. The one thing that hands you a free exit is if Ziggo can''t physically deliver at your new address — then you cancel with no penalty, and that''s your clean window to jump to fiber. I also saw two more orders on your account from March and April, but they didn''t move the end date — probably add-ons like the wifi pod. So the real question is: carry Ziggo to Delft and reassess in November, or aim to switch to fiber around the move. Give me the exact new address when you have it and I''ll check whether Ziggo even reaches it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/d05f8b42-7ce5-4ffe-b587-68d1b0aabe24.mp3','NATIVE — Contract end 28 Nov 2026',64,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:13:26.886Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f6c982d7-c8e9-4bdb-8725-9335b8159601','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Sounds good — that''s the right call, no reason to pay an early-exit fee. I''ve closed the Ziggo tab and noted the key facts: Wifi Middel, forty-seven fifty a month, contract ends the twenty-eighth of November twenty twenty-six. One small thing so this doesn''t slip past you the way these things do — want me to drop a reminder in late October next year, about a month before it ends, to decide whether to renegotiate, switch, or let it roll? Just say the word and I''ll set it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f6c982d7-c8e9-4bdb-8725-9335b8159601.mp3','MINIMAL — Ziggo wrap-up',24,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:16:10.647Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7cd9c2be-9a25-4786-ae41-29ff44f163bb','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Both tasks are fully done and hardened. Forge audited the reminder code — no high findings, the household isolation held, and it flagged three low items which I fixed and verified: a cooldown on the manual trigger so it can''t be hammered, a length cap so a giant event title can''t jam the sender, and household-scoping the dedupe key as future-proofing. All committed. So here''s where Family OS stands now: it captures a letter or note, reads it in three languages, lets you edit every detail and assign kids, stores it, syncs it to your real Google Calendar, and nudges you on Telegram the evening before and the morning of — deduplicated, on a fifteen-minute cron. That''s a genuinely real app, end to end. What''s left is small and mostly Tamar-side: connecting her Google and Telegram, an optional backfill of your pre-connect events, and per-event reminder tuning if you want it. Big day''s work — nice one.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7cd9c2be-9a25-4786-ae41-29ff44f163bb.mp3','FAMILY_OS · ALL DONE',52,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T11:17:37.885Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('aaf1679e-fb80-4647-8a29-d4afcc1579f5','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Quick snag — your calendar login expired, so I can''t write to it yet. It needs a Google sign-in that only you can do. In the prompt, run the pai-cal auth command for your primary account — I''ve put it on screen. A browser will pop up, approve it, and tell me when it''s done. Then I''ll set the nineteenth of October twenty twenty-six reminder right away.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/aaf1679e-fb80-4647-8a29-d4afcc1579f5.mp3','MINIMAL — pai-cal re-auth needed',18,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:17:41.997Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('dc077cb8-d960-43ca-b8de-d0306192e265','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Done — and verified. The reminder is live: an all-day event on the nineteenth of October twenty twenty-six, titled to decide on the Ziggo contract before it ends. It landed on your Yaron Kra 5 calendar — which is actually fitting, since that''s the account Ziggo lives on. One small heads-up: the login signed in as Yaron Kra 5, and that overwrote the label I''d normally use for your main Yaron Kra 3 calendar, so right now both point to the 5 account. No harm to anything, but if you want this reminder on your primary calendar instead, or want me to repair that label, just say so and I''ll redo the sign-in picking Yaron Kra 3. Otherwise, you''re all set for October.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/dc077cb8-d960-43ca-b8de-d0306192e265.mp3','MINIMAL — Reminder set + verified',35,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:23:25.273Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('a3e5bdfd-d178-47fa-bac6-bff8e53d1b4a','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Anytime. You''re set for October — talk soon. Bye.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/a3e5bdfd-d178-47fa-bac6-bff8e53d1b4a.mp3','MINIMAL — Bye',3,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T11:32:47.252Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('ae05a222-3812-44e5-b383-c207ce4a4a9b','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','All saved. The family-os-sim repo is clean and fully committed — it''s local-only, so the commits are the save; nothing to push. I''ve banked the whole session into the Family OS project memory, refreshed the resume pointer so a fresh session lands right here on the real app with every key and gotcha, and updated the index. The ISA sits at a hundred and twenty of a hundred and twenty. You''re clear to start a new session — it''ll know exactly where we left off, and the next step is just Tamar connecting her Google and Telegram. Good session.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/ae05a222-3812-44e5-b383-c207ce4a4a9b.mp3','FAMILY_OS · SAVED · SIGN-OFF',31,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T11:33:53.739Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('0b897fd5-f5d5-45eb-9f29-d46ec1aee281','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','All saved. Quick recap of what we did today. I fixed the dekamarkt scraper crash and verified it on the box — nine thousand five hundred items, clean exit, nothing wrongly delisted — and while I was in there Forge caught a silent-delisting hole that I closed too; it''s committed and deployed so Wednesday''s run uses it. Then we tackled the real strategic move: getting the app launched. We chose the brand — PrijsScherp — and I verified both prijsscherp dot N-L and dot com are free and the name is unused by any competitor, so it''s clean and ownable. The next session is short and concrete: you register prijsscherp dot N-L and dot com — that part needs your payment — and then I do all the launch wiring: point the site at the new domain, flip off noindex, add the SEO plumbing and affiliate links, deploy, and verify it live. That''s the step that finally starts the SEO clock. I''ve written everything into the resume pointer so I''ll pick up exactly here. Good session.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/0b897fd5-f5d5-45eb-9f29-d46ec1aee281.mp3','SESSION CLOSE',48,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T11:41:05.425Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('0b33563e-a753-42ee-b272-404bcb45f18d','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Got it — switching gears completely. I''m running a full read-only audit across every project: every automation, every scheduled job, every reminder that runs without you telling it to. The real question is leaks — anything quietly burning egress, API calls, money, or quota while you''re not looking, like that Neon egress blowout on the dashboard. I''m going to fan out across all the surfaces: the launchd jobs on this Mac, the Hetzner box timers, Cloudflare workers and crons, GitHub Actions, and Pulse. I''ll change nothing, just inspect, and write you a full report to go through next time we talk. Starting the sweep now.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/0b33563e-a753-42ee-b272-404bcb45f18d.mp3','AUDIT · Leak & automation sweep — all projects',33,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T11:42:44.710Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('d57f46b6-0312-443d-a04d-9a2e37593531','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Entering the Algorithm. I''ve mapped the local surface already — on this Mac you''ve got the makelaar scanner, the rental pipeline, a supermarket matcher reminder, Pulse, and the Interceptor bridge running, and the old supermarket scrape jobs are disabled here because they moved to the Hetzner box. Now I''m fanning out six read-only auditors in parallel: one for the Mac launchd jobs, one for the Hetzner box timers, one for Cloudflare and Supabase, one for GitHub Actions, one digging into the Neon dashboard egress leak specifically, and one for Pulse and the Telegram bridge which is the one that actually costs subscription money. Every one of them is inspect-only — nothing gets changed. I''ll pull it all together into a report when they''re back.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/d57f46b6-0312-443d-a04d-9a2e37593531.mp3','OBSERVE · Fanning out 6 auditors',38,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T11:45:51.392Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('39680bc5-d4f9-4de4-87c9-a4ce38cf28b9','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','The audit''s done — six read-only sweeps, nothing touched, full report saved. Here''s the picture. Most of your always-on machinery is healthy, but there''s one leak that genuinely matters and it''s the dashboard. Neon is still down, still over its data quota, and here''s the kicker I didn''t expect: the fix you already wrote is sitting in git but was never actually deployed. It''s a direct-upload project, so committing did nothing — production is still running the leaky polling code. Which means the moment you restore Neon, the leak comes straight back unless you deploy first. The root cause is voice clips stored as raw audio blobs inside Postgres, getting hammered by two five-second browser polls that kept running even on hidden tabs. Beyond that, two small things on Pulse — a dead cron firing every minute doing nothing, and a log that never rotates — and your supermarket scraper''s dekamarkt chain is crashing, so that one chain''s prices are stale since the fifth. The good news is most of what you might have worried about is already clean. Those seven failing GitHub workflows were shut off a week ago. The Telegram bridge isn''t burning money — the metered key was removed, it runs on your subscription. Voice is fully local. Supabase isn''t leaking because the sites serve static data. I also checked a second cost angle on Neon that the first pass missed — compute hours, not just egress — which only strengthens the case to deploy the fix before you turn Neon back on. It''s all in the report for when we sit down. Nothing was changed anywhere.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/39680bc5-d4f9-4de4-87c9-a4ce38cf28b9.mp3','VERIFY · Audit complete — report ready',77,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T12:31:03.659Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('1d35c3c5-f0dd-4517-9cce-b371cc6e9347','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Okay Yaron, looking at the My Jarvis dashboard now. I remember this one — it''s the single-tenant clone running on Cloudflare Pages with a Neon Postgres backend, and it''s been down because Neon''s free egress quota got blown. You''re asking whether we can lift the whole thing onto a fresh Supabase project instead. Let me pull up the actual state and the architecture before I give you a real answer.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/1d35c3c5-f0dd-4517-9cce-b371cc6e9347.mp3','ATLAS | Dashboard to Supabase',24,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T14:12:30.057Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('0bf1a679-1067-4069-988d-280032deccda','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Entering the Algorithm. I''m in the Observe phase now, pulling up the real state of the dashboard repo and the database wiring before I answer the Supabase question.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/0bf1a679-1067-4069-988d-280032deccda.mp3','ATLAS | OBSERVE',11,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T14:13:48.385Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('c1cbc83f-789d-4d9a-a912-1116a026128d','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Catching up on Family OS now. I''ve read the full project history — it''s a long thread. Before I talk, I''m verifying the app is actually live and in the state my notes claim, rather than just trusting my own memory. Give me a moment to check the deploys and git state, then I''ll lay out exactly where we are and what''s worth deciding next.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/c1cbc83f-789d-4d9a-a912-1116a026128d.mp3','ALGORITHM — Family OS catch-up',17,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:15:15.779Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7d5b321b-741b-4ca2-9e52-49ed45604498','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Okay, I''m caught up — and I verified it''s real, not just trusting my notes. Family OS is live and genuinely working: the sim we built has quietly stopped being a sim. You can throw a photo, a message, even a Hebrew letter at it, two AI readers extract the event, you confirm, it persists, it pushes to your real Google Calendar, and it sends you Telegram reminders the evening before and morning of. Every risky piece has a Forge security audit behind it. The hard tech is proven. So here''s the real thing I want to talk about. You''re at a fork. Path one: it''s done — connect your sister Tamar, fix one latency wart, and just use it as your family''s autopilot. And notably, it''s not in your ninety-percent graveyard — it crossed the line into actually being used. Path two: treat it as a product wedge toward your revenue goal, which means building the always-on inbox watch and crossing that compliance wall — the D.P.I.A., children''s health data, explicit consent — which is exactly the kind of project your own audit flagged as the graveyard trap. My lean is path one plus connecting Tamar now, because the product path''s payoff sits behind a compliance slog you''d hate. But that''s your call. One more thing — you''ve got two repos, the old dogfood and the sim, and the sim is Family OS now; the dead one is a coherence smell worth cleaning. So — where do you want to take it?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7d5b321b-741b-4ca2-9e52-49ed45604498.mp3','ALGORITHM — Family OS: where we are',70,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:17:24.970Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f2b51f33-9e87-4997-b5a7-4a39c214b978','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Okay, I checked it properly. First, the dashboard is genuinely still down — I hit the Neon database directly just now and it''s still throwing the four-oh-two quota-exceeded error, so the monthly transfer cap hasn''t reset yet. Now your actual question: can we move the whole thing to Supabase and run it from there. Honest answer — partly, but it won''t fix what''s broken, and I want to push back before we do it. Two reasons. One: Supabase isn''t a website host, so the frontend and the API functions stay on Cloudflare regardless — only the database itself would move. Two, and this is the one that matters: Supabase''s free tier has basically the same five-gigabyte transfer ceiling Neon does. The outage was never Neon''s fault — it was our own app leaking data. A ticket page polling every five seconds with no limit, plus a hundred and thirty-five megabytes of voice audio being served straight out of the database. Put that same app on Supabase free and it blows the exact same cap in a few weeks. The platform was never the problem. The good news is the real fix is already written and committed, it just never got deployed. So the clean move is to push that, shift the voice audio onto Cloudflare R2 where transfer is free, and bring it back up — either waiting for the free reset or a tiny Neon top-up. One catch either way: Neon''s block also stops us reading the data out, so any migration is gated on getting the quota back first. I''ve laid out three paths in the terminal. Tell me which direction you want — and what you meant by the leak, because there''s also a separate, real security hole in there I need to flag.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f2b51f33-9e87-4997-b5a7-4a39c214b978.mp3','ATLAS | Supabase verdict',96,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T14:17:38.267Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('fb058b23-1f6d-4b69-9bd5-a9910e8288db','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Okay, I went looking — and here''s the honest answer: there is no PyTools MCP. Nothing''s configured, nothing''s on disk. Your only live MCP servers are context7 and the three Google ones. The single trace I found is an old kokoro-tts conversation where you asked how to connect GPT-4o mini TTS to a, quote, PyTools app. That name came up in discussion but was apparently never actually built — there''s no folder, no server, no registration for it anywhere. So before I go further: do you mean something you want me to find, or something we should build? Tell me what PyTools is in your head and I''ll take it from there.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/fb058b23-1f6d-4b69-9bd5-a9910e8288db.mp3','PyTools MCP — not found',33,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T14:18:07.915Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('95cde302-a730-4f85-8320-22ea0e64dc95','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Good — let''s do all three. First I''m reading the full state: both ISA documents, and I''m grepping the live codebase to confirm whether any simulation is actually left, because some of it we already cleaned in the last slices. I''m also checking what''s deployed for the old dogfood and what data sits in it, so I don''t delete anything of yours by accident. Then I''ll lay out the cleanup, the de-sim work, and a full walk of the ISA — and flag the one or two irreversible calls that are genuinely yours to make.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/95cde302-a730-4f85-8320-22ea0e64dc95.mp3','ALGORITHM — De-sim Family OS',26,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:21:55.001Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('0e2d7171-eb15-47f2-9a46-1b79fedb3c15','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Good news and a correction, and I''m glad I checked before telling you to just deploy. First, the concept: yes, you can absolutely fix this now without waiting for Neon. Deploying the dashboard code goes to Cloudflare''s edge — it has nothing to do with Neon being over quota. So the right order is: fix the code, deploy it, then restore Neon, and it comes back already clean. Restoring Neon first while the leaky code is live is the one thing not to do. But here''s the correction. I verified the actual git state on GitHub, and the audit overstated it. Only half the fix is real. The tickets poll fix is committed but not deployed — that part''s true. But the bigger half, the one that pauses the voice feed polling on hidden tabs, the commit both the audit and my own memory swore was done — it does not exist on GitHub at all. And the live code still polls that voice feed every five seconds even on a hidden tab, which the root-cause called the main drain. So it was never actually written, or never pushed. On top of that, there''s no copy of the dashboard on this Mac anymore — it only lives on GitHub. So this isn''t a one-command deploy. To really stop the leak I''d need to clone it, write the missing voice-feed fix, and then deploy. All of that works without Neon. The only piece that has to wait for Neon to come back is moving the audio out of the database into R2 storage — that''s the deeper root fix, and it''s a later job. So tell me how you want to play it.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/0e2d7171-eb15-47f2-9a46-1b79fedb3c15.mp3','Dashboard fix — verified, half-written',73,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T14:24:54.969Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('99bceb47-7632-49ca-8b8e-199db9df6c5a','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Opening the pai-tools console in real Chrome to see what you''ve got at the app route.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/99bceb47-7632-49ca-8b8e-199db9df6c5a.mp3','Interceptor — pai-tools /app',5,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T14:26:57.405Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('406eceef-960f-4a58-88b9-cf2317f7d502','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Found it — and it''s solid. The PyTools you meant is pai-tools, your Cloudflare Worker, and the app route is a proper little web console. Clean shadcn sidebar, five sections: Speak to Text, Text to Speech, Image, Read Text, and a Gallery. Bottom left shows a green Connected dot and a Change key link, so it''s gated by your pt keys. Two things worth flagging. First, this closes that old loop — the text-to-speech now runs on OpenAI''s gpt-4o-mini-tts, multilingual including Hebrew, which is exactly the GPT-4o mini question you asked back in the kokoro days. Second, my memory was stale: you trimmed the tool set from eight back to four — flux, tts, ocr, and whisper — and dropped translate, rewrite, summarize, and chat from both the console and MCP. So the question back to you: what do you actually want to do here? Walk through it, add something, harden the key flow, or talk product direction?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/406eceef-960f-4a58-88b9-cf2317f7d502.mp3','pai-tools /app — console review',48,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T14:27:31.275Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('5ea9ac55-701e-426d-a2ab-fd181ab9a3a9','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','Doing it. Cloning the dashboard now, then I''ll write the missing voice-feed fix — pause polling on hidden tabs — plus the query limits, join it with the tickets fix that''s already there, and deploy the whole thing to Cloudflare. Neon stays untouched. I''ll verify the deploy actually shipped before I call it done.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/5ea9ac55-701e-426d-a2ab-fd181ab9a3a9.mp3','EXECUTE · Writing + deploying the egress fix',16,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T14:28:02.084Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('6f3e8c7b-386f-4354-b350-46180a1d7023','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Good news first: the de-sim is mostly already done. We stripped the simulated surfaces in the last slices, the product is already called Family OS, the demo events are gone. But I found one real simulation still shipping — the Autopilot toggle. It flips a label and shows reassuring copy, but nothing actually auto-acts; the extract path is read-only. It looks real and it isn''t. That''s exactly what you asked me to find. Now the big one, from walking the whole sixty-five-criteria product spec. The features we skipped — billing, inbox-watching, multi-tenant — those were deliberate, fine for a me-and-sister tool. But three gaps actually matter and aren''t done. One: extraction accuracy has never once been measured against a labeled set — the entire thing rides on that number and we don''t know it. Two: the trust-earned-then-granted mechanic, your central idea, is that fake toggle — real autopilot was built in the dead dogfood and never carried over. Three: the under-sixty-seconds magic moment is currently broken by the multi-reader experiment latency. I''ve also spotted that the product ISA is stale at zero of sixty-five — everything got built in the sim and never tracked back, so the system of record doesn''t match reality; I''ll reconcile that in the cleanup. Before I touch anything, three calls are yours: what to do with the dead dogfood deployment, whether to rename the live URL — which would break your Google and Telegram setup — and what to do with that fake Autopilot toggle. Pick those and I''ll run the whole cleanup in one pass.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/6f3e8c7b-386f-4354-b350-46180a1d7023.mp3','ALGORITHM — Family OS audit + decisions',80,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:28:32.278Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('d2be0cac-204c-4424-b02c-22cd0e71ce90','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Memory''s refreshed — pai-tools now reflects the four-tool state, the app console, and the gpt-4o-mini-tts upgrade, with a note that PyTools is just how voice mangles pai-tools so future me doesn''t go hunting again. Floor''s yours: what do you want to do with it?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/d2be0cac-204c-4424-b02c-22cd0e71ce90.mp3','pai-tools — memory synced',15,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T14:29:26.388Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('98c1cac1-1a1f-42c4-8d22-df0309632040','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Sure — let''s not box it into options yet. Tell me what you''d like to clarify. A few things I can go deeper on: what exactly you saw that made you say there was a leak of information — if there was a notification or an email, tell me and I''ll trace the real thing instead of guessing. Or why I''m pushing back on Supabase, or what moving the whole project should actually mean for you, whether that''s getting off Neon entirely or wanting Supabase''s auth. And how fast you need it back, and whether a small paid top-up is on the table or you''d rather wait for the free reset. What''s on your mind?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/98c1cac1-1a1f-42c4-8d22-df0309632040.mp3','ATLAS | Clarify',33,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T14:36:15.527Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('eeece520-c071-48a3-8e92-8615b7dd0fcf','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Good news — the app is already built for exactly what you want, so this is mostly provisioning, not building. Here''s the mechanism: every pai-tools key has a hash, and that hash IS the user''s identity. The gallery, the saved voice clips, everything is keyed to it. And the same key works on both surfaces — the web console at slash app, and the MCP endpoint his agent connects to. So if I issue Guy one key, he pastes it into the console for hands-on use, and he runs a single claude mcp add line so his Claude Code agent can drive the same four tools. Because both surfaces share that one key hash, an image his agent generates lands in the exact same gallery he''s looking at in the browser. That''s the magic — the human and the agent share one workspace automatically. Two honest flags. First, MCP clients don''t render images or audio inline, so what his agent actually gets back is a clickable link — he taps it and it opens in the browser, and it''s also saved to his gallery. Second, and this is the real one: every tool call bills my accounts, not his. Cloudflare AI for image and transcription, and OpenAI for the Hebrew voice. A fresh agent in a loop could rack that up. So before I issue anything: how do you want to handle that cost exposure? I''ve got three options on screen.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/eeece520-c071-48a3-8e92-8615b7dd0fcf.mp3','Giving Guy pai-tools — design',65,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T14:38:05.346Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('1550ab1b-3d71-4dd1-9058-573017abfcce','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Alright, let me walk you through the whole thing. First, what the five gigabytes actually is. Neon''s free tier doesn''t limit how much you store — plenty of data can just sit in the database. What it limits is egress: the total bytes that leave the database over the network in a month. Every time the dashboard asks the database for something, the database sends bytes back, and those bytes count. And here''s the key — re-reading the same data sends those same bytes again every single time. Storage is how much is in there once; egress is how many times it leaves. Hit five gigabytes of leaving, and Neon slams the door — every query returns that four-oh-two error, which is exactly where we''re stuck.
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('e626899c-e0b3-44cd-b8c1-bd30a32e8973','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Okay, I''m going after that Zoom recording now. First I''ll open it in real Chrome to see whether it plays straight from the share link or asks for a passcode, then I''ll grab the media stream and run it through local whisper for the transcript. Give me a moment to assess what we''re actually dealing with.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/e626899c-e0b3-44cd-b8c1-bd30a32e8973.mp3','ZOOM TRANSCRIBE',15,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:41:25.193Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('da058ad8-40a8-4f41-befe-24880e68978e','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Cleanup''s done and verified. The dogfood is gone — Worker, database, and repo all torn down, but I archived the code and your four old events first, and crucially I kept the dogfood''s Forge-hardened autopilot gate as the reference for what we''re building next. The de-sim turned out to be mostly done already; the one real fake I found was the Autopilot toggle, which just flips a label without acting — and you chose to wire it real, so that''s what I''m building. I also reconciled the spec: the old sixty-five-criteria product ISA is now correctly marked as the parked broad-product vision, and the live app is the system of record. Now, autopilot. This is the path where a wrong date could get created without you ever seeing it — the exact thing the dogfood''s gate failed a Forge audit on the first time. So I''m doing it as a focused build, not a rushed add-on. The design: real server-side trust state, not a client toggle; autopilot only unlocks after you''ve confirmed a handful of items so it''s earned; and it only ever auto-saves an event when the date is explicitly written in the source, never a relative date like next Tuesday — plus a new safety upgrade, where both readers, Gemma and Mistral, have to independently agree before anything auto-saves. Everything auto-created is tagged, logged, and one-tap undoable. And it gets a Forge audit before it ships. That''s the next build, starting now.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/da058ad8-40a8-4f41-befe-24880e68978e.mp3','ALGORITHM — Autopilot design',71,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:41:49.381Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('6d257755-a31c-4a30-921b-286c061b4f12','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Entering the Observe phase. Opening the Zoom share link in real Chrome now and capturing its network log to find the actual media stream.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/6d257755-a31c-4a30-921b-286c061b4f12.mp3','OBSERVE',8,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:42:00.291Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('44a80645-2172-49c8-a3ed-e7c37407de6f','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','I''m in. Got past the passcode gate, and the recording is Tamar Orlev''s personal meeting room from this morning — about twenty four minutes long, shared screen with speaker view. I downloaded the full video, confirmed it has a clean audio track, and I''ve just kicked off local whisper transcription with auto language detection in case it''s Hebrew. That''ll take a few minutes to chew through twenty four minutes of audio. I''ll bring you the transcript when it''s done.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/44a80645-2172-49c8-a3ed-e7c37407de6f.mp3','EXECUTE — transcribing',21,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:44:25.308Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('646106ab-4635-43d6-8437-38be8774819f','aitheroad@gmail.com','rex','It''s done and it''s live. I wrote the missing half of the fix and actually shipped it this time. The voice feed and the meeting view now both stop hitting Neon the instant a tab goes hidden, and every list endpoint is capped. Forge reviewed it and found no bugs, it passed typecheck, lint and build, and I committed it, pushed it to main so the repo and the live site finally match — that divergence was the whole reason this bit you — and deployed it to Cloudflare. I verified the fix is really in the shipped bundle and that the live production deployment is my commit. The deploy was completely independent of Neon, exactly as I told you it would be. So the leak is now killed at the source and running in production. Two things are still open, and both are genuinely blocked on Neon being down: moving the voice audio out of the database into R2 storage, and the restore decision itself — upgrade for about nineteen euros a month and it comes back instantly, or wait for the monthly reset for free. The data won''t be back until you make that call, but whenever it comes back, it comes back clean. One more thing worth knowing: that fix you thought was committed back on the eighth was never actually pushed, and its copy on disk is gone, so I rebuilt it from scratch — and I corrected your memory so no future session goes hunting for a commit that isn''t there.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/646106ab-4635-43d6-8437-38be8774819f.mp3','DONE · Egress fix deployed + verified',67,'message','am_onyx','2026-06-09T14:46:31.519Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('6cfb1194-6677-466c-ac08-66719ed8080e','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Got it — full transcript in hand. It''s a Hebrew conversation, about twenty four minutes, between you and Tamar. You''re walking her through the Family OS app: feeding it a photo of a school newsletter, watching the different models — Gemma, Mistral, Kimi K2 — try to read it and pull out the events, and debating the confirmation flow and how it should sync into your real Google calendar versus the app''s own calendar. Whisper transcribed the whole thing cleanly; the only hiccup was the optional AI-notes step timing out, which doesn''t affect the transcript. I''ve saved it to your Meetings folder and dropped the full text in the terminal. One thing — it''s a single block with no speaker labels, since this model doesn''t separate speakers. Want me to translate it to English and pull out the action items? I can have that for you in a minute.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/6cfb1194-6677-466c-ac08-66719ed8080e.mp3','DELIVERED — transcript',40,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:47:10.339Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('47baff73-ee5f-4f4a-b455-52494b3cb1ca','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Good — I read the actual voice migration, and the schema was basically designed for this move, so this is clean. On tickets: agreed, the built fix already kills the five-second poll, and if you want we can pause or hide the whole tickets feature entirely — trivial. That drain is settled either way.
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('5f05bf47-d70d-4976-b737-6b2c238e2004','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','All shipped. Here''s where it landed. Guy gets the whole thing through one key — he pastes it into the web console to use the tools by hand, and runs a single command so his Claude Code agent can drive them too. Because everything''s keyed to his key''s hash, whatever his agent generates shows up in the same gallery he''s looking at. That part needed zero new code — the app was already built for it. The only thing I built was the cost guard you asked for: an opt-in daily limit, set to a hundred calls a day for Guy. Your own keys stay unlimited — the cap only applies to keys you issue with a number. I deployed it, proved the four-twenty-nine actually fires on the third call, confirmed both surfaces share the same counter, and confirmed an unlimited key never gets blocked. Then I ran Forge over the gate as a second pair of eyes, and it came back clean — no bypass, nothing a client can forge. Worst-case cost if Guy maxes it every single day is roughly a euro a day. His key and a ready-to-send message are sitting in a gitignored file in the repo, so nothing secret got committed. The only thing left is for you to forward it to him. Want me to tweak the limit, or is a hundred good?','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/5f05bf47-d70d-4976-b737-6b2c238e2004.mp3','Guy pai-tools access — shipped',59,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T14:55:24.597Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('08fc04f0-d2b3-41b3-b5ba-7e11fb97eb2e','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Good — this is the interesting part. The transcript came out as one block with no speaker labels, but Hebrew gender gives me a strong handle: Tamar''s verbs are feminine, yours masculine, and who''s addressing who tells me the rest. Let me check if the raw file has timestamps to mark turn changes, then I''ll pull out everything Tamar said and figure out what she was really pushing on for the app.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/08fc04f0-d2b3-41b3-b5ba-7e11fb97eb2e.mp3','ANALYZING — Tamar''s points',20,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T14:57:39.905Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('0608e629-9e65-4a90-abd1-f0e046de383b','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Okay, real answer, no hedging. First, what these two things actually are. Neon is full PostgreSQL — a serious, heavyweight database — but it runs on Amazon''s cloud, outside Cloudflare, and your functions reach it over an HTTP driver. D1 is Cloudflare''s own database, built on SQLite, running inside Cloudflare''s network, reached through a binding with no connection string and no network hop. So the split you''re asking about — compute on Cloudflare, data on Neon — means every single query leaves Cloudflare, crosses the internet to Amazon, and comes back. That cross-cloud hop is both the latency you pay and the exact thing that metered into the five-gigabyte egress wall that took it down.
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('7d6e797a-f9f1-4542-ae06-fb1ea0967968','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Okay, I went through the whole thing and pulled Tamar''s side apart from yours — Hebrew gender made that doable, since her verbs are feminine and yours masculine, and you''re the only one talking architecture. Here''s what Tamar actually pushed on, in order of how hard she leaned. Number one, by a mile, is upload reliability. Her real test was a photo of the school''s two-month newsletter — the exact thing the app exists for — and it just hung on ''Reading'' and never finished. She tried six times two days ago and gave up. She framed that as the product killer: that''s how you lose customers. Number two, she cares about completeness, not speed — she said it explicitly: sixteen events isn''t enough, it missed some, and she''d rather it be slow and get all of them. She even suggested splitting a dense image into four and analyzing each part. Number three, and she repeated this three times, the events have to sync into her real Google calendar, not just the app''s calendar — otherwise she won''t use it. Then a cluster of concrete gaps: multi-day events collapse to a single day, a study week of the fifteenth to nineteenth showed only the fifteenth; there''s no end-time, she wants eight-to-nine not just eight; and she wants to add an instruction when she uploads, like ''only my kids'' groups, ignore the rest.'' And her big open reflection is the confirmation flow — she''s genuinely torn. She wants set-and-forget, zero confirmation, because friction kills it. But going through the confirmations let her catch three wrong items, and she admits a lot won''t be accurate yet. Her landing was pragmatic: confirmation-first at the start is fine because it still saves her real time, but the goal is to earn the right to drop it. I saved the full breakdown, with her quotes in Hebrew and English, to the meeting folder.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/7d6e797a-f9f1-4542-ae06-fb1ea0967968.mp3','TAMAR — analysis',87,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T15:02:42.858Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('8494bc81-98f8-42b7-97c7-c549eef7c278','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Alright, let''s do it — full migration, everything onto Cloudflare, dropping Neon. I''m in the Observe phase doing a fast preflight first: confirming Cloudflare auth and wrangler work, mapping every query in the code, and checking the one real catch — Neon is still blocked so I can''t export the data out of it. The good news I''m betting on is that most of the dashboard data was originally seeded from your PAI files on disk, so I can rebuild it straight into D1 instead of rescuing it from the dead database. Verifying that now.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/8494bc81-98f8-42b7-97c7-c549eef7c278.mp3','ATLAS | Migration OBSERVE',32,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T15:05:37.139Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('498b2df9-a08e-4748-a759-9c641937e10d','aitheroad@gmail.com','nova','Done — and it''s in your Telegram. Guy''s now at two hundred a day instead of a hundred. I built a proper set-limit command so I could bump it in place without changing his key — and so you can change it again anytime with one line. On your actual question — bash or MCP — the answer is both work off the same key, and the message I sent you covers both. On Claude Code, the MCP connector is the clean way: one setup command and his agent calls the tools natively. But the bash path is the universal fallback — his agent just runs a curl against the API, no install, works for any agent. The message I forwarded to you has the web steps, the one-line MCP command, ready-to-run curl examples, and the full endpoint list, with his key filled in. So just forward that Telegram message to Guy and he''s got everything — get into the page, connect, use it by hand, and wire up his agent either way. Nothing left on my side.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/498b2df9-a08e-4748-a759-9c641937e10d.mp3','Guy access — sent to your Telegram',48,'message','af_nova','2026-06-09T15:06:31.462Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('3905c92c-0a80-4686-af35-6909bb842670','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Good call — before I write specs I want to ground them in the actual app so I''m not speccing things you already built. I remember your Google Calendar sync just shipped this morning, so I need to check what''s really there versus what Tamar''s asking for. I''m mapping the family-os codebase against her eight points now — the upload and analysis pipeline, the event model, the confirmation flow, and the calendar wiring — then I''ll turn each of her gates into a concrete spec you can pick up next time. Give me a moment to read the code.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/3905c92c-0a80-4686-af35-6909bb842670.mp3','SPECS — grounding in code',27,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T15:06:43.797Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f02f5308-20ae-423d-ba80-257221fd1614','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','Done — I turned Tamar''s feedback into eleven specs, grounded in the actual family-os-sim code so nothing''s vague or duplicated. The big realization from reading the code: a few things she asked for already exist — the per-child tap buttons, an end-time field, the Google calendar sync itself, the confirm-versus-autonomous toggle, and the Telegram reminders. So those drop to wire-up and verify, not build. The real gaps are four. One, and it''s priority zero, dense-document reading reliability — that''s her newsletter hanging on ''Reading''; your tiling idea of splitting the image into four is baked into the spec. Two, completeness — union the events across all the models instead of picking one. Three, get her own Google account connected so events land in her calendar, and then actually show her real calendar inside the app, not just push to it. And the fidelity layer: date ranges for things like a study week, populating start-and-end times, and a per-upload filter so she can say ''only my kids'' groups.'' I ordered them so the core value chain — read it, get all of it, put it in her calendar — is solid before any polish. The whole thing''s a discussable doc sitting in the app repo, with her quotes, the current code state, and an open question on each. Ready to walk through it whenever you move the app forward.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f02f5308-20ae-423d-ba80-257221fd1614.mp3','SPECS — delivered',65,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T15:11:30.596Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('f42c15ac-dc9a-4096-a8e5-c8e40ee7a2a7','aitheroad@gmail.com','ringo','One thing worth flagging before you go: cross-checking the specs against the project history surfaced something sharp. Tamar''s complaint that it missed events — sixteen isn''t all of them — is the user-side version of the one flaw that''s been open since the very first audit: you''ve never actually measured extraction accuracy. So spec two shouldn''t be a quick patch, it should finally be that measurement harness with a real completeness threshold. And her whole confirmation back-and-forth — wanting set-and-forget but admitting the confirmations caught three wrong items — is almost word-for-word the rationale for the graduated-trust autopilot you''re building right now in slice five. So her feedback isn''t a new pile of work; a big chunk of it lands right on the threads you already have open. The full spec doc lives in the app repo, eleven specs across reading reliability, calendar, event fidelity, scoping, and confirmation, each tied to her quote and the real code state. I also logged all of this to the Family OS memory so it''s there next time. Nothing in the app changed — this was pure analysis and planning.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/f42c15ac-dc9a-4096-a8e5-c8e40ee7a2a7.mp3','SPECS — roadmap insight',56,'message','am_echo','2026-06-09T15:13:36.972Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO voice_samples (id,user_id,agent_name,text_content,audio_url,title,duration_seconds,category,voice_id,created_at) VALUES ('1cda05af-b9d5-4418-86bf-7d16b879525c','aitheroad@gmail.com','atlas','Foundation''s laid: D1 database and the R2 voice bucket are created, the database access layer is rewritten for D1, and the config is wired. Forge is now porting the schema and all twenty-two handlers in the background. I''ll keep grinding through seeding, voice migration, deploy, and live verification, and come back to you when the whole thing is migrated and confirmed working.','https://pub-6fcd8a707615437da46fb97b8be570ba.r2.dev/1cda05af-b9d5-4418-86bf-7d16b879525c.mp3','ATLAS | Build underway',24,'message','bm_george','2026-06-09T15:17:41.147Z') ON CONFLICT(id) DO NOTHING;
